 "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.3", "title": "the sign is a Leibniz sign", "statement": "After a gauge by the 3-colouring the sign of a pair is the product of the local turns delta, the sign of a term in an incidence determinant. The real sign is prod_t delta(r(t), s(t)).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.C.x1", "title": "sign as a product of two dimer weights", "statement": "Write the local phase as alpha(r(t)) beta(s(t)) and get Z as a product of two incidence determinants.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "At a face with three non-root corners the two cyclic triple products of the phase have ratio -1, and any separated weight gives ratio 1. Disjointness of r and s is what stops the sum from being one determinant.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: One black triangle with three non-root corners.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.C.4", "title": "height-function form of J", "statement": "The Q_s-reversal can change the cycle structure of D completely and J still moves by exactly 2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C2"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Suggests J(r, s) = g(s) - g(r) plus a term local to Q_s, like a dimer height.", "test": "Fit g on the enumerated pairs of the n = 15 and n = 23 examples.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.K.O", "title": "involution: reverse a cycle of Q_s", "statement": "Cycles of Q_s are directed by r. Reversing one chosen from s alone changes r, keeps the weight and flips the sign. T classifies all components: the number of partners is 0 or 2^k.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.2; L iota_1; T beta, Prop. 2.1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.1", "title": "twisted incidence determinant of Q_s", "statement": "For fixed s the partner sum is kappa det N_s, where N_s is the incidence matrix of Q_s reduced at the roots. It vanishes exactly when Q_s has a cycle. Lemma 5.2 is 'the rows of an incidence matrix around a cycle are dependent'.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C1; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Prop. 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.K.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.2", "title": "support of the multivariate polynomial", "statement": "With one variable per incidence, F(w) has coefficient +1 or -1 on each tree matching and 0 on every other state. So CT F(w)F(1/w) is the number of tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x12", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.3", "title": "quartic Berezin integral", "statement": "F(w) is a two-species Grassmann integral with one quartic term per black face. It has an exact Gaussian decoupling, with no assured sign.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.K.c", "title": "checked on every cyclic second state", "statement": "Every state with a cycle in Q_s has zero signed partner sum; the partner count is 2^k or 0 on 140358 states (comb/lab/extra2.py 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "eviden