ed objects", "statement": "Weights are signed crossings of vertical rays. A sign-reversing involution on lists of cmin marks; its fixed points share a sign. For cmin > 1 three verifications are left to the reader (dep/audit-li.md).", "where": ["L Section 4, Defs 14, 20-23, Appendix B"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T1", "title": "integer polynomial per exchange component", "statement": "Integer weights 0 <= a <= 6n; Z_C(z) = sum eps z^omega has a nonzero coefficient of (z - 1)^m. Every exchange component contains tree pairs of both signs.", "where": ["T Lemma 5.1, Thm 5.2, (11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T2", "title": "marked walk (Garsia-Milne)", "statement": "Alternate the two involutions on tokens; the walk ends at a tree pair or restarts with fewer D-cycles. Never computes cmin. 2^O(n log n) time.", "where": ["T Thm 5.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.H", "title": "heights as test functions, no weights", "statement": "Test the signed measure against a product of cmin heights at white faces. Pairs with one D form a cube, partners of one s form a cube, and the product is a cmin-fold difference that survives only on covers with exactly cmin cycles.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Sections 2-3 (Theorem B); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REWRITTEN-PROP-5-1.md (self-contained rewrite by the referee)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x7", "rel": "refutes"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.lin", "title": "linear weights 1 + x a", "statement": "Replace e^{xa} by 1 + xa. The polynomial has degree at most n and the same leading coefficient; on the forest side it is a signed elementary symmetric moment. The Lean proof uses the same polynomial (lean/DIFFERENCES.md item 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 7; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/SIGNIFICANCE.md Section 2 (full proof with real signs and parity only)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every 