th a pair and fewer than 2^cmin tree matchings; start at 17 vertices with cmin = 3.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}, {"to": "p.D.2", "rel": "generalizes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.4", "title": "exactly one tree matching is impossible", "statement": "The signed unweighted sum over tree matchings is zero, so their number is even. The cube has two.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2 (after T Thm 5.2)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x2", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.5", "title": "tree matchings can be exponentially rare", "statement": "Gluing q hexagonal-prism duals into white faces gives 3^q states and 2^q tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (rarity); code/rarity.py q <= 6; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/PROOF.md Prop. 6 (states, pairs and tree matchings multiply under insertion into a white face)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.U.x3", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.6", "title": "a canonical forest pair", "statement": "Under a bijection from states to trinity arborescences, tree matchings have a tree description that singles one out.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md step 3"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Write the Hine-Kalman bijection on the 12-vertex class 6 example where every extremal rule fails, and look at the images of its 8 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.1", "title": "prescribed-degree spanning tree of H", "statement": "[y^{d*}] det L_H(y) is the number of tree matchings: a positive coefficient of the tree-degree polynomial. Existence would follow from a support theorem for that polynomial.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 1, 4"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.2", "title": "label-transversal white trees", "statement": "Tree matchings are the spanning trees of the restricted white-face graph whose edge labels use every t and every v once. A doubly squarefree coefficient of a Laplacian determinant counts them, by Cauchy-Binet with all terms n