, "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.C.x1", "title": "sign as a product of two dimer weights", "statement": "Write the local phase as alpha(r(t)) beta(s(t)) and get Z as a product of two incidence determinants.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "At a face with three non-root corners the two cyclic triple products of the phase have ratio -1, and any separated weight gives ratio 1. Disjointness of r and s is what stops the sum from being one determinant.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: One black triangle with three non-root corners.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.C.4", "title": "height-function form of J", "statement": "The Q_s-reversal can change the cycle structure of D completely and J still moves by exactly 2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C2"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Suggests J(r, s) = g(s) - g(r) plus a term local to Q_s, like a dimer height.", "test": "Fit g on the enumerated pairs of the n = 15 and n = 23 examples.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.K.O", "title": "involution: reverse a cycle of Q_s", "statement": "Cycles of Q_s are directed by r. Reversing one chosen from s alone changes r, keeps the weight and flips the sign. T classifies all components: the number of partners is 0 or 2^k.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.2; L iota_1; T beta, Prop. 2.1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.1", "title": "twisted incidence determinant of Q_s", "statement": "For fixed s the partner sum is kappa det N_s, where N_s is the incidence matrix of Q_s reduced at the roots. It vanishes exactly when Q_s has a cycle. Lemma 5.2 is 'the rows of an incidence matrix around a cycle are dependent'.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C1; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Prop. 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.K.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.2", "title": "support of the multivariate polynomial", "statement": "With one variable per incidence, F(w) has coefficient +1 or -1 on each tree matching and 0 on every other state. So CT F(w)F(1/w) is the number of tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x12", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.3", "title": "quartic Berezin integral", "statement": "F(w) is a two-species Grassmann integral with one quartic term per black face. It has an exact Gaussian decoupling, with no assured sign.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.K.c", "title": "checked on every cyclic second state", "statement": "Every state with a cycle in Q_s has zero signed partner sum; the partner count is 2^k or 0 on 140358 states (comb/lab/extra2.py 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.K.x1", "title": "choose the cycle using r", "statement": "Let the reversed cycle depend on the partner.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (disk identity and bijectivity)"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The reversal changes r, so a rule that reads r need not pick the same cycle on the way back. The choice must be a function of s. No smallest counterexample was searched.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: none recorded; the argument is a proof that the involution property can fail, not an instance", "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.O", "title": "Taylor coefficient of order cmin", "statement": "Unit circulations from dual paths, a slide of edges onto spokes, Z(x) = sum over D of prod (-i e^{xL+} + i e^{xL-}); the coefficient of x^cmin is a nonzero multiple of a positive sum.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.3, (5.3)-(5.5)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.L", "title": "second involution on marked objects", "statement": "Weights are signed crossings of vertical rays. A sign-reversing involution on lists of cmin marks; its fixed points share a sign. For cmin > 1 three verifications are left to the reader (dep/audit-li.md).", "where": ["L Section 4, Defs 14, 20-23, Appendix B"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T1", "title": "integer polynomial per exchange component", "statement": "Integer weights 0 <= a <= 6n; Z_C(z) = sum eps z^omega has a nonzero coefficient of (z - 1)^m. Every exchange component contains tree pairs of both signs.", "where": ["T Lemma 5.1, Thm 5.2, (11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T2", "title": "marked walk (Garsia-Milne)", "statement": "Alternate the two involutions on tokens; the walk ends at a tree pair or restarts with fewer D-cycles. Never computes cmin. 2^O(n log n) time.", "where": ["T Thm 5.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.H", "title": "heights as test functions, no weights", "statement": "Test the signed measure against a product of cmin heights at white faces. Pairs with one D form a cube, partners of one s form a cube, and the product is a cmin-fold difference that survives only on covers with exactly cmin cycles.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Sections 2-3 (Theorem B); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REWRITTEN-PROP-5-1.md (self-contained rewrite by the referee)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x7", "rel": "refutes"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.lin", "title": "linear weights 1 + x a", "statement": "Replace e^{xa} by 1 + xa. The polynomial has degree at most n and the same leading coefficient; on the forest side it is a signed elementary symmetric moment. The Lean proof uses the same polynomial (lean/DIFFERENCES.md item 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 7; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/SIGNIFICANCE.md Section 2 (full proof with real signs and parity only)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.id", "title": "spoke weights are a height function", "statement": "omega(s) is the volume under the height of s, and L+(C) - L-(C) is the number of white faces inside C, which is B + 1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 2.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.N.c", "title": "leading coefficient checked exactly", "statement": "The first nonzero coefficient equals the signed sum of products of enclosed face counts on every instance tested.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/supplemental.py (49 groups); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/code/linear.py; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 5 (71224 rooted triangulations up to 18 vertices)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/supplemental.py (49 groups); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/code/linear.py; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 5 (71224 rooted triangulations up to 18 vertices)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x1", "title": "zero, vertex-only or face-only weights", "statement": "Use weights alpha_t + beta_v, or none.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/data/zero_weights.json; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Such weights are pure gauge: every state has the same total, and the signed count is 0 = 0. What is needed is positive circulation on cycles, not positive weights.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Cube (octahedron dual, 6 vertices): two pairs with J = +1 and -1, Z = i - i = 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x2", "title": "parity or mod p count without weights", "statement": "Show the number of tree matchings is odd, or nonzero mod p.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 8; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/TABLES.md (residues mod 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The number of tree matchings is always even (the two signs balance), and T = P - 2 N_1 mod 4 is compatible with T = 0. The weighted sum is the refinement that works; the first degree at which anything survives is cmin. No modulus among 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11 gives a universally nonzero residue; the positive counts seen are 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 22.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Octahedron: 2 tree matchings, signed count 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x3", "title": "tree pair among the fewest-cycle pairs", "statement": "Among the pairs with the fewest D-cycles one has Q_s a forest; or every cycle cover D has a forest orientation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D2; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 7 (E2d, E3); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md O3 (a 40-vertex one-cycle cover with no tree pair)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Reversals inside one fixed cycle cover cannot be guaranteed to reach a forest pair, so a proof must move between covers. The leading coefficient is nonzero because of the fewest-cycle covers, but the surviving pairs can live in other covers. A statement that held on 1794 cases failed at the next size. (Scope as corrected by the referee.)", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 16 vertices, class 158, t0 = (2,7,3): a single 13-cycle whose two orientations both have a triangle in Q_s; its 12 tree matchings lie in two other covers. Also the octahedron with every face split in four (n = 15).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x4", "title": "highest or lowest partnered state", "statement": "The top (bottom) partnered state of the lattice is a tree matching.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 4 (E1, E1c); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md O1 (extremes of the whole matching lattice fail at 10 vertices)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "For an extreme s every D has all cycles one way, but reversing a cycle of Q_s changes the number of D-cycles by two and extremality does not forbid it.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3) for the highest state, and its mirror image for the lowest (the referee's correction: the author's enumeration identified reflections and reported 14).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x5", "title": "minimal cover, all cycles one way", "statement": "Take D with cmin cycles and orient all of them counterclockwise (or clockwise).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 5 (E2, E2c); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The leading coefficient sums over all minimal covers and prefers no orientation.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3) for counterclockwise, and its mirror image for clockwise (referee's correction; the author reported 13).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x6", "title": "largest rank difference", "statement": "The pair maximising omega(s) - omega(r) is a forest pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 6 (E5)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Maximality forces the cycles of Q_s to be counterclockwise and nothing more.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x7", "title": "one cycle always suffices", "statement": "cmin = 1, so a first-order argument is enough.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 13"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "cmin reaches 3 without separating triangles (192 of 3374 rooted cases up to 16 vertices) and 4 with them. A first-order argument is not enough and Li's Appendix B is needed. Unboundedness of cmin is not proved.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 9 vertices: octahedron with an octahedron glued into a face, cmin = 2.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x8", "title": "cubes of tree matchings; sign = parity of rank", "statement": "Tree matchings split into cubes of dimension cmin; or eps(s) = (-1)^omega(s) up to a constant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 9, 10"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Z(q)/(q - 1)^cmin can have mixed signs, which refutes a rank-compatible signed cube decomposition. An abstract partition into cubes of dimension cmin is refuted by cardinality (referee).", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Signs: 14 vertices, class 24, face 6, Z = -1 + 2q + q^5 - 2q^6. Cardinality: a 13-vertex instance with 6 tree matchings and cmin = 2 (refc/code/cube_cardinality.json). Sign = parity of rank fails at 8 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x9", "title": "ordinary determinant, all face variables 1", "statement": "Evaluate det(sum_t M_t) with no coefficient extraction.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md, data/exact_determinant.json; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/IDENTITIES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Without extraction a black face can supply two transitions and another none; the extra terms can cancel the answer. Testing only the cube or the octahedron would have hidden this.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual (8 vertices): squarefree coefficient 45/64 at z = 5/4, all-one evaluation 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x10", "title": "allow doubled edges (standard double dimers)", "statement": "Add a diagonal so that r and s may share edges, as in Kenyon's double-dimer determinant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 3; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Nonvanishing becomes too easy: F_lambda(1) = lambda^n times the number of states, which is positive even with no pair. An SL2 connection does not kill doubled edges.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: A rooted 9-vertex gluing with 4 states, no pair, doubled value 4.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x11", "title": "positive semidefinite blocks", "statement": "Find a gauge in which the local matrices M_t are positive semidefinite, then use mixed-discriminant positivity.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Each block is, after multiplication by i, Hermitian of trace zero and rank two, signature (1, 1, 0). No similarity or congruence changes that. The determinant explains the cancellation and does not replace the planar positivity.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Any black face with two or three non-root corners.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x12", "title": "Combinatorial Nullstellensatz", "statement": "Get a nonzero evaluation of F from the coefficient form of Alon's theorem.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Naming a nonzero monomial of F already names a tree matching. Substituting w = a_t b_v kills F.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Any instance: F(a_t b_v) = 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x13", "title": "real stability of the tree-state polynomial", "statement": "The unsigned generating polynomial of tree matchings is real stable, like spanning-tree polynomials.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Projecting onto matchings destroys stability.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Cube: abc + def vanishes at a = b = c = e^{i pi/6}, d = e = f = i.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.1", "title": "mixed determinant with positive curvature", "statement": "Z = [prod z_t] det(sum z_t M_t) is n! times a mixed discriminant of rank-two blocks. Prove it nonzero from structural hypotheses.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D1; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "At a = 1 the matrix is the adjacency matrix of T[X] with a U(1) connection of holonomy i around black and -i around white triangles.", "test": "Compute rank(sum over S of W_t) against |S| on cases with and without pairs; look for a non-diagonal normalisation.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.2", "title": "2-adic evaluation at z = -1", "statement": "Choose weights with every L+ - L- odd and evaluate T's polynomial at -1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "A count mod powers of 2 that sees the weights.", "test": "Check on the examples whether such weights exist and the value is nonzero.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.3", "title": "cycle popping, random walk", "statement": "The two moves pop cycles of Q_s and of D, as in Wilson's algorithm. Show the walk hits a tree pair fast.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D4; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md (exchange walks)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "All 320 random and greedy trials from ten bad starts ended within ten moves (con, COMPUTED, small sample).", "test": "Measure hitting times on exchange components of growing size; look for a potential.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.4", "title": "Pfaffian gadget for the turn tensor", "statement": "Replace each black face by a planar matchgate with signature q^delta on distinct ordered corners and zero on equal corners.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 6; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would remove the coefficient extraction and give a polynomial-time evaluation.", "test": "Check the Grassmann-Pluecker identities of the six-value signature with the boundary order fixed.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.5", "title": "height potential on pairs", "statement": "A combination of the two state heights that decreases along some exchange move at every non-tree pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 7"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would turn existence into descent.", "test": "Search for a non-tree local minimum of each candidate on small exchange graphs.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.6", "title": "curved double-dimer connection, Lee-Yang", "statement": "Realise the loop factor -i e^{xL+} + i e^{xL-} as the trace of a non-flat connection.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 15; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 8"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Each loop factor is -2i e^{xm} sinh(x Delta/2); zeros lie on the imaginary axis loop by loop.", "test": "Solve the connection equations on two bipyramids and test trace identities on nested loops.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.7", "title": "LGV after cutting along seams", "statement": "Cut the pair diagram into non-intersecting paths and use a Lindstrom-Gessel-Viennot determinant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 8"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "A fixed path matrix would make the sum a single determinant.", "test": "Do the cut on the cube and on the first instance with two D-cycles.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.8", "title": "abstract valuation theorem", "statement": "Axiomatise: a finite signed cycle system, two involutions, a positive circulation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 17"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would say which planar hypotheses do the work.", "test": "List the axioms and find the first one that fails on a torus or a disk with four roots.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.N.9", "title": "a test function with one sign on all covers", "statement": "There is a test function of s for which every cycle cover contributes with the same sign, so that no minimum over the number of cycles is taken.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md, open question 2"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "On the 479 cases with more than 2^cmin tree matchings (comb/data/rows_v16.json), search low-degree polynomials in the heights.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.10", "title": "flux on a small set of faces", "statement": "Put positive flux only on a set of faces that meets the interior of every feasible D-cycle.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md (economical weights)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Smaller weights, smaller degrees.", "test": "Compute minimum hitting sets of cycle interiors on the enumerated instances.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.D.1", "title": "two evaluations of one sum", "statement": "Supported on forest pairs, and not zero.", "where": ["O Prop. 5.1; L Key Lemma 7; T Thm 5.2"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.2", "title": "at least 2 cmin tree matchings", "statement": "The signed measure on tree matchings kills all polynomials of degree below cmin in the rank, and the two signs are equally frequent.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Corollary 3"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.3", "title": "at least 2^cmin tree matchings", "statement": "Every rooted triangulation with a pair has at least 2^cmin tree matchings. True for all 5088 cases up to 16 vertices; equality in 4609.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 11; labyrinth/scatter.json"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Find a rooted triangulation with a pair and fewer than 2^cmin tree matchings; start at 17 vertices with cmin = 3.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}, {"to": "p.D.2", "rel": "generalizes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.4", "title": "exactly one tree matching is impossible", "statement": "The signed unweighted sum over tree matchings is zero, so their number is even. The cube has two.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2 (after T Thm 5.2)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x2", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.5", "title": "tree matchings can be exponentially rare", "statement": "Gluing q hexagonal-prism duals into white faces gives 3^q states and 2^q tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (rarity); code/rarity.py q <= 6; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/PROOF.md Prop. 6 (states, pairs and tree matchings multiply under insertion into a white face)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.U.x3", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.6", "title": "a canonical forest pair", "statement": "Under a bijection from states to trinity arborescences, tree matchings have a tree description that singles one out.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md step 3"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Write the Hine-Kalman bijection on the 12-vertex class 6 example where every extremal rule fails, and look at the images of its 8 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.1", "title": "prescribed-degree spanning tree of H", "statement": "[y^{d*}] det L_H(y) is the number of tree matchings: a positive coefficient of the tree-degree polynomial. Existence would follow from a support theorem for that polynomial.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 1, 4"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.2", "title": "label-transversal white trees", "statement": "Tree matchings are the spanning trees of the restricted white-face graph whose edge labels use every t and every v once. A doubly squarefree coefficient of a Laplacian determinant counts them, by Cauchy-Binet with all terms nonnegative.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 5; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 3"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.3", "title": "three-matroid intersection", "statement": "A tree matching is a common basis of the stated three matroids. The natural triple is irredundant. This does not rule out a different two-matroid encoding or a min-max theorem.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 6; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md Section 1"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.4", "title": "unique partner: |det K_{B-s}| = 1", "statement": "Zeroing the entries of s in K_B gives a determinant equal to the number of partners up to sign. A tree matching is a state where it is 1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 2 (after T Prop. 2.1)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.5", "title": "tree matchings = partnered Hamiltonian cycles", "statement": "Tree matchings are in bijection with the Hamiltonian cycles avoiding e0* whose state has a partner. So 3 #TM <= #HC(G).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Prop. 7; research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md Thm 7.2 (explicit left inverse; image = partitions with acyclic white parent map)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_limits, 2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.A.x1", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.6", "title": "rooted functional orientations; two-sided hypertrees", "statement": "Two more exact restatements of the target, as an orientation problem and as a simultaneous hypertree realisation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 5, 7"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x1", "title": "matching matroid meets graphic matroid", "statement": "Treat the two endpoint constraints as one matroid and use Edmonds' two-matroid intersection.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 6; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/data/other_candidates.json; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/REFEREE-constructive.md"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Matchings are not a matroid (augmentation fails on K_{2,2}). With only the face partition and the white graphic matroid, the augmenting-path algorithm returns white trees that repeat vertices.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism: 4 of the 6 common bases of the two-matroid relaxation are not states (referee's correction, refd). Larger witness: truncated octahedron, eleven spokes repeating non-roots 3 and 4 (con/data/other_candidates.json).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x2", "title": "unconstrained white spanning trees", "statement": "Every spanning tree of the white-face graph, or of its restriction to duals of B, gives a tree matching.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md (wilson_candidate)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Both label constraints are needed. Rejection sampling accepted 0 of 100 trees on the larger named graphs.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Octahedron: 128 white trees, 8 after restricting to duals of B, 2 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x3", "title": "trinity arborescences = tree matchings", "statement": "The Hine-Kalman bijection carries all states to arborescences; perhaps every arborescence is a tree matching.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md (trees and trinity)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Arborescences count all states. Tree matchings are a proper subset with no known one-colour criterion.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual: 3 arborescences in each colour, 2 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x4", "title": "Yutsis partition of G", "statement": "Identify the two induced trees with a Yutsis decomposition of the cubic graph.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 11"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Different ground sets: the vertices of G against the vertices of T.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: definitional", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.1h", "title": "support of the tree-degree polynomial", "statement": "Show the target degree vector d* lies in the support of det L_H(y), from plane incidence inequalities.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 2; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P8, P9"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "An unsigned target: no cancellation to explain. If every lattice point of the degree polytope were realised (P9), convexity would finish.", "test": "Enumerate H-trees on the cube and the hexagonal bipyramid; compare the support with the lattice points of its convex hull.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.2h", "title": "spanning-tree parity / matroid parity", "statement": "'Each black centre keeps exactly two of its three spokes' looks like the spanning tree parity problem that Feder and Subi solve in polynomial time for 2- and 3-sided faces.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/REPORT.md (leads); research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 10"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "If it is a matroid parity instance, Lovasz gives a polynomial algorithm, against 3^(N/4).", "test": "Design the gadget for one black centre and two adjacent centres; enumerate feasible parity solutions against partial spoke choices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.hist", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.4h", "title": "Bernardi process, Schnyder woods, blossom trees", "statement": "A canonical tree or orientation of the map might produce a tree matching directly.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 4, 11, 12, 13"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Each theory uses three colours and rooted trees on triangulations, as the target does.", "test": "On the octahedron and the hexagonal bipyramid, test every facewise corner rule for bijectivity on X and for the forest condition.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.5h", "title": "order-theoretic position in the state lattice", "statement": "Outcome (topo): the tree matchings are neither an interval nor an antichain of the clock lattice, and the top and bottom states are often tree matchings. No order-theoretic pattern was found.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P6; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 9"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Decided on the topology agent's sample (166 lattices); a description of the subset is still missing.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.6h", "title": "describe partnered Hamiltonian cycles in G alone", "statement": "There is a description, without states, of the Hamiltonian cycles of G avoiding e0* whose state has a partner.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md, open question 3"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "For the hexagonal prism list the 2 partnered and 2 unpartnered avoiding cycles and compare their face sequences; then test any candidate rule on the 176726 unpartnered cycles of the survey.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.R.1", "title": "out-degree count", "statement": "A tree component with v vertices and a roots has v - a out-edges and v - 1 edges, so a = 1. T: s is a tree matching iff it has exactly one partner.", "where": ["O Lemma 6.1; L Lemma 8; T (3), Prop. 2.1, Thm 1.2"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.R.c", "title": "unique partner checked on 140358 states", "statement": "Brute force over all states: tree matching iff exactly one partner; the partner count is 2^k or 0.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/extra2.py 16; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/extra2.py 16; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.R.x1", "title": "a forest state is enough", "statement": "Call s good as soon as Q_s is acyclic, with no partner assumed.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (forest versus rooted forest); research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.5"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Without the partner the out-degree count is unavailable: a component can hold two roots and another none. 'Forest', 'cycle-breaking' and 'tree matching' agree for pairs and differ for single states.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual: all 3 states have acyclic Q_s, only 2 are tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.E.1", "title": "tree-cotree duality", "statement": "The duals of the deleted spokes form a spanning tree on the white faces.", "where": ["O Lemma 2.1; L Cor. 27; T 7.1"], "tags": ["step E"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.E.2", "title": "Temperley / Kenyon-Propp-Wilson", "statement": "Read the step as the tree-to-matching bijection of KPW.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md E2; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step E"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "KPW applied to the white graph encodes all its spanning trees and carries the label constraints along; it does not identify those dimers with B (dim).", "test": "Write the bijection for the octahedron and the n = 15 example.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.E2.1", "title": "orient towards y0", "statement": "Each tree edge is assigned to its end farther from y0 and selects the side of its black face bordering that end.", "where": ["O 6.1; L Claim 31; T 7.1"], "tags": ["step E2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.E2.2", "title": "the three papers select the same P", "statement": "Li's trace of the dual tree through black vertices gives the same set of edges of G.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/