, "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.R.Lean", "title": "add a sink at the third root (Lean)", "statement": "Out-degree at most one and no directed cycle make a forest; no component count.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/DIFFERENCES.md item 20"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.Lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.E.Lean", "title": "the white tree is never built (Lean)", "statement": "The formal proof selects P inside G and skips the tree on the white faces.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/DIFFERENCES.md item 19"], "tags": ["step E"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.Lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.F.Lean", "title": "cut-balance lemma against the disk identity (Lean)", "statement": "A directed cycle of selected edges is a state cycle; a cut all of whose edges lie in a perfect matching contradicts |cut| = 2|black cut| + 3. No induced trees, no Jordan curve.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/DIFFERENCES.md items 21-22"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.Lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.G.Lean", "title": "glue perfect matchings across the 3-cut (Lean)", "statement": "Strong induction on the H- form: a perfect matching containing e with connected complement. Splitting is contraction.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/DIFFERENCES.md items 23-25"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.Lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.G2.c", "title": "the Lean proof builds here; standard axioms only", "statement": "#print axioms gives propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. No sorry, admit, axiom or native_decide in the 31 files.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 1; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/build/axioms.out (Lean 4.34.1, Mathlib d13f23b7)"], "tags": ["step G2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 1; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/build/axioms.out (Lean 4.34.1, Mathlib d13f23b7)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.G2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.HC", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.A.GT", "title": "one exact Euler identity, both directions", "statement": "m - b - (2p - 4) = (1/2) sum over non-face regions of (beta - (d - 4)). Every region contributes at most 0 except a black-inner separating triangle, which contributes +1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md Lemma 2.2, Thm 2.1"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC)"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.U.x5", "rel": "refutes"}, {"to": "th.A.T", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.A.6", "title": "pairs are alpha-orientations (Felsner lattice)", "statement": "Pairs up to reversing D-cycles are the alpha-orientations of H - t0 with out-degrees 2, d_x - 2, d_r - 1. They form a distributive lattice.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md Lemma 3.1"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC)"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.A.5", "title": "Hall-free shelling construction", "statement": "Build a pair by a canonical ordering from t0 inward, as for Schnyder woods.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md F2"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "The certificate of non-existence is always one triangle, which is how density conditions behave when a shelling exists.", "test": "Implement a shelling of the 55 triangulations up to 14 vertices and compare with the flow pairs.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x5", "title": "LP relaxation of the three constraints is integral", "statement": "Perfect matchings of B intersected with complements of spanning trees of H form an integral polytope.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md M1-M4; posed in research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 5"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The natural LP is not integral. This does not exclude all encodings of the special spoke class; the broad hardness result is under polynomial Turing reductions.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: A half-integral vertex at 13 vertices; minimality not proved. A feasible completion has one tree state and one non-tree state (structure referee INTEGRATION.md).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x6", "title": "induction by degree-4 expansion", "statement": "Lift a tree matching through the expansion of a degree-4 vertex.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md I1; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "States lift bijectively, but the lift of a tree matching is a tree matching only under a side condition at the split vertex that is not inherited. Contraction can create the obstruction.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Contraction creates a black-inner triangle from 11 vertices on; not every tree matching lifts (708 of 1516 cases in gt/ROUTES.md I1).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x7", "title": "positivity of the norm or of the Laplacian terms", "statement": "CT F(w)F(1/w) and the constrained Laplacian coefficient are sums of nonnegative terms, so they are positive.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/REPORT.md; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 6"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Both are positive exactly when F is not zero, and showing that is the paper's argument. The positivity in the proof sits on the D side, these on the s side.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Obstructed roots of the double octahedron (9 vertices): 360 restricted white trees, 16 with one spoke per face, no tree matching.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x8", "title": "tree count as an unrooted invariant", "statement": "The number of tree matchings equals a fixed evaluation of a Tutte, Penrose, Tait or flow invariant of G.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/REPORT.md; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/invariants.json"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The count depends on the root.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: plantri graph 12_2: 2 or 8 tree matchings depending on the black root, all roots with a pair.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x14", "title": "single-swap descent on the number of Q-cycles", "statement": "From every pair with a cycle in Q_s some single exchange lowers the number of cycles.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md D1, D2"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "A swap along a Hamiltonian D-cycle exchanges r and s, so it cannot lower the count both ways. Exhaustive data up to 15 vertices had made it look true.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 50 vertices, 4-connected (gt/code/data/deeptrap_50_1.json); two swaps suffice there.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x15", "title": "a global sign gauge on incidences", "statement": "Flip signs of incidence variables so that all tree matchings get the same coefficient sign.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/REPORT.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "A GF(2) inconsistency certificate: six tree states in which every incidence appears an even number of times, three with negative sign.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: A 13-vertex instance with six tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.N.11", "title": "non-increasing exchange path to a tree pair", "statement": "From every pair there is a path of exchanges along which the number of Q-cycles never increases and reaches 0. A sign-free form of T Theorem 5.2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md D3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Search exchange graphs at 20 to 30 vertices for a pair with no non-increasing path; at 80 vertices look for pairs with no decrease within two swaps.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.N.12", "title": "Li's marked objects are the e_m coefficient", "statement": "Li's objects with cmin distinct marks are the elementary symmetric reading of the linear-weight coefficient.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/REPORT.md (still open)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Enumerate Li's objects on an instance with cmin = 2 and compare the signed count with the coefficient of x^2 in F(1 + xa) for unit marks.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.5", "title": "parity is enough three times; the value 3 once", "statement": "In the real-sign form, reversing a Q_s-cycle or a D-cycle multiplies the sign by (-1)^length. So the cancellation, the forest lemma and the permutation sign need only that state cycles are odd. The value 3 is needed once, to align the signs of the minimal D groups.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/SIGNIFICANCE.md"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.C.x1", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.7", "title": "extremes of Felsner's lattice of pairs", "statement": "The claim that one of the two true lattice extremes always carries a forest pair is reported refuted. Independent replay is pending.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_conjectures/PREDICTIONS.md items 1-2"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Single-face terminal orientations need not be lattice extremes; even the true two extremes are reported insufficient. Test distance-one and irreducible replacements.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Reported at 18 vertices: 26 rooted instances in two triangulations. Provisional computation, no final report yet.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.conjectures", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.D.8", "title": "finding a tree matching is in PPAD", "statement": "Each phase of the marked walk follows a path in a graph of degree at most 2 with alternating signs.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/REPORT.md (leads)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would place the search problem between polynomial time and the 3^(N/4) enumeration.", "test": "Write one phase of T Theorem 5.3 as an END-OF-LINE instance with polynomial-size circuits for the two involutions.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G.5", "title": "sharp primal hypothesis; gluing at black-inner cuts", "statement": "In G the obstruction is a non-trivial 3-edge cut whose black-ended side avoids b0. Li's cyclic 4-edge-connectivity is sufficient and not sharp: 1714 of 4494 rooted instances with separating triangles still have pairs.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md G"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC)"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.B.6", "title": "combinatorial Gauss-Bonnet with signed angles", "statement": "The state defines a flat signed-angle structure, and a vertex-local identity says turning equals minus colour winding. The disk identity is then the theorem of turning tangents. Orientation-free form: every chosen-edge disk has W = B + 1. Independently AI-refereed in the topology referee report; human checking pending. Apply the referee corrections where relevant. The proof uses Euler counting, not a smooth turning-tangents theorem. Boundary flatness and exclusion of the outer face are required.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/REPORT.md item 1; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/ROUTES.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology"], "date": "2026-11-14", "verdict": "Named claim checked with corrections in REFEREE.md; human check pending. Newly announced RAINBOW.md proof not inspected."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.4", "title": "cancellation as a Morse matching", "statement": "Pairs are combinatorial vector fields, tree pairs are gradient fields, and the cancellation reverses a closed orbit. The matching is acyclic and its critical cells are the forest pairs. Its Euler characteristic Z(1) is always 0, so a graded version is needed. Independently AI-refereed in the topology referee report; human checking pending. Apply the referee corrections where relevant. Correct grading: J = J_ccw - 2 times the number of clockwise Q-cycles. Pair each root with its outer-centre spoke in the Forman reading. Numerical checks of the Boolean levels only reach k <= 1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/REPORT.md item 2; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology"], "date": "2026-11-14", "verdict": "Named claim checked with corrections in REFEREE.md; human check pending. Newly announced RAINBOW.md proof not inspected."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.F.6", "title": "Alexander duality: #cycles = 1 + b1(P)", "statement": "The complement of the 2-factor retracts onto P, so the number of cycles is one more than the first Betti number of P. Independently AI-refereed in the topology referee report; human checking pending. Apply the referee corrections where relevant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/REPORT.md item 2; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology"], "date": "2026-11-14", "verdict": "Named claim checked with corrections in REFEREE.md; human check pending. Newly announced RAINBOW.md proof not inspected."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.7", "title": "sutured Floer support; point-rainbow white trees", "statement": "A tree matching exists iff a named spin-c structure is supported in the sutured Floer homology of the special alternating link of G (Juhasz-Kalman-Rasmussen), iff the white faces have a 'point-rainbow' spanning tree. Independently AI-refereed in the topology referee report; human checking pending. Apply the referee corrections where relevant. The referee announces a Rado/Euler proof of the point-rainbow criterion in RAINBOW.md, but that file was not yet present when integrated; that new proof was not inspected here.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/REPORT.md item 3 (conditional on T Thm 1.2); COMPUTED on 826 instances up to 16 vertices; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology"], "date": "2026-11-14", "verdict": "Named claim checked with corrections in REFEREE.md; human check pending. Newly announced RAINBOW.md proof not inspected."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.7h", "title": "local search from a point-rainbow tree", "statement": "Same-colour exchanges from a point-rainbow tree, never increasing the black excess, reach a tree matching. A proof would be a cancellation-free local-search proof of the key lemma.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/REPORT.md item 4 (R6'); 450 of 450 instances up to 16 vertices"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Measure plateaus and step counts at 18 to 20 vertices (1543 triangulations at 18); look for a potential such as black excess plus a white-tree distance.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.D.x1", "title": "the partner of a tree matching is a tree matching", "statement": "Swapping r and s would then be a free involution on tree matchings and explain why their number is even.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/REPORT.md item 5"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The evenness is a signed cancellation, Z(1) = 0, and not a free involution. Forest pairs are not symmetric in r and s.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 6 failures among 442 tree matchings tested (topo data; smallest instance not recorded here).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.U.c", "title": "cycle-to-state map replayed; it is not injective", "statement": "Every Hamiltonian cycle avoiding e0* gives a state, and that state is a tree matching or has no partner. Two cycles can give the same unpartnered state: on the hexagonal prism 4 avoiding cycles give 3 states, on the rim-8 bipyramid 6 cycles give 4 states.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_labyrinth-map/spotcheck.py (bipyramids of rim 4, 6, 8, every edge of t0)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_labyrinth-map/spotcheck.py (bipyramids of rim 4, 6, 8, every edge of t0)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.map", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G.6", "title": "boundary states of a cut; complete at lengths 3 and 4", "statement": "Cut T along a cycle, record a finite boundary state on each side, glue: the number of Hamiltonian cycles is the linear term of a Temperley-Lieb pairing of two disk vectors. O Theorem 2.2 says every piece with triangular boundary realises all 3 boundary patterns; for quadrilaterals all 6 patterns allowed by a parity rule occur (conditional on O; one sub-case by a finite computation).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/PROOF.md Prop. 1, Theorem 3; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/CATEGORICAL.md"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.G.x2", "title": "a uniform boundary condition for longer cuts", "statement": "Induct along cuts of length 5 or more with a boundary condition that every piece satisfies.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/PROOF.md Prop. 4; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/EXPERIMENTS.md"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The realised boundary patterns depend on the piece from length 5 on. The prescribed edge is the complete boundary datum of a triangular cut, and that is why the induction stops at separating triangles.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: A piece with 9 vertices and a 5-cycle boundary (cat data); checked up to 13 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.A.x2", "title": "two roots instead of a root face", "statement": "Root at two vertices not tied to a face; every root pair then has a two-root tree matching, and it gives a Hamiltonian cycle.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/REPORT.md (what failed); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/CATEGORICAL.md"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Two roots move the obstruction and do not remove it, and O Lemma 6.2 needs all roots on one side of every selected cycle, which a root face guarantees. This is what the face root is for.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Existence: plantri graph 12_6, 51 of 66 root pairs. Recovery: a two-root tree matching with no Hamiltonian cycle at 8 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.K.x2", "title": "the two cube structures form a bicomplex", "statement": "Treat reversal of Q-cycles and reversal of D-cycles as two commuting differentials and read the proof as homology.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/REPORT.md (what failed)"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The two reversals do not commute. The homological packaging is a restatement and gives no new existence argument.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 of 624 pairs up to 12 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x9", "title": "topological Hall for partial tree matchings", "statement": "Get a tree matching from connectivity of the complex of partial tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/REPORT.md (what failed)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The complex is not connected enough even in the smallest case.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Octahedron: a two-face subcomplex is disconnected.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.TG.7", "title": "acyclic triangle factor of a second trinity K", "statement": "Hamiltonian cycles with a root on each side are the acyclic triangle factors of a second trinity K built from T. A symmetric restatement of the goal.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/PROOF.md Prop. 5"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.8h", "title": "every Hamiltonian cycle from a two-root tree matching", "statement": "With two roots allowed to vary, the state method sees every Hamiltonian cycle.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/REPORT.md (table); COMPUTED up to 12 vertices"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Decide it at 13 to 16 vertices; if it holds, find the modified disk identity for cycles that separate the roots.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.9", "title": "contraction inequality tau(T) >= tau(T/ac)", "statement": "Contracting a degree-4 vertex never increases the number of tree matchings. An injection behind it would lift tree matchings along vertex splits.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/REPORT.md (table); 948 contractions"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Look for a local rule extending a tree matching across a vertex split on the 948 cases (cat/code/recursion.py contract).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G2.primal", "title": "primal proof with flows and real signs", "statement": "A full primal route using disk cut counts, linear-weight nonvanishing, recovery and 3-cut gluing. Author audit and finite checks exist; independent review pending.", "where": ["proofs/research/2026-11-14_astra_primal-proof/PRIMAL-PROOF.md; proofs/research/2026-11-14_astra_primal-proof/STATUS.md"], "tags": ["step G2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.primal", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.HC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G2.drafta", "title": "draft A: heights proof", "statement": "Manuscript route through signed intersection heights. The draft referee reports FOLLOWS with sentence repairs; this entry does not certify that every repair is applied.", "where": ["paper/draft-A/barnette.tex; research/2026-11-14_opus_review-draft-A/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step G2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.drafta", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.HC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G2.draftb", "title": "draft B: scalar height moments", "statement": "A manuscript route entirely in T. It uses the scalar height moment sum epsilon times omega(s)^m and an m-fold finite difference, then recovers via the tree of faces Y_s from Q_s plus two root sides. No plane spoke graph is needed. Author audit exists; final independent review pending.", "where": ["paper/draft-B/barnette.tex; research/2026-11-14_opus_manuscript-B/REPORT.md"], "tags": ["step G2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.draftb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.HC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.families", "title": "exact even-prism counts", "statement": "For a prism of order 4m: m states, two tree matchings, c_min=1 and normalized polynomial z^(m-1)-1. Full proof supplied, independent review pending.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_counting-families/FAMILIES.md Section 1"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.families", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.ext1", "title": "distance one from a lattice extreme", "statement": "Some element at rank distance at most one from a true extreme carries a forest pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_conjectures/PREDICTIONS.md item 3"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Enumerate true extremes and their rank-one neighbours through 24 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.conjectures", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.ext2", "title": "join or meet irreducible pair cover", "statement": "Some join-irreducible or meet-irreducible lattice element carries a forest pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_conjectures/PREDICTIONS.md item 4"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Enumerate irreducibles and all cover orientations through 22 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.conjectures", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.TG.older", "title": "older approaches: tests in progress", "statement": "The final report gives a radial/permeating-tree dictionary and rejects a direct identification with H-s. A direct Pfaffian transfer still lacks balanced incidence objects, disk identity and recovery.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_older-approaches/BRIDGES.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_older-approaches/REPORT.md"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "A classical reduction could transport the missing root data.", "test": "Replay the named prism, truncated-octahedron and Pfaffian tests when the report is available.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.older", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.N.li-check", "title": "Li two-mark involutions on running example", "statement": "213 marked objects; iota1 fixes 141, iota2 fixes 9 of one sign; signed count -9. Closure, involutivity and sign reversal checked exhaustively on this instance.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_audit-digestions/code/verify.py; outputs/verification.json"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_audit-digestions/code/verify.py; outputs/verification.json"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.map", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.B.height", "title": "signed white area is additive", "statement": "The referee supplies a winding-number proof of height equals signed white area without separating triangles. This new proof has not itself had a second referee.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/REFEREE.md Section (h)"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.reft", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.unbounded", "title": "unbounded c_min in Goodey chains", "statement": "End-rooted chains of k octahedra have k D-components in every pair, while primal faces have size four or six. Separating triangles are allowed. Author proof, not yet independently refereed.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_older-approaches/BRIDGES.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_older-approaches/REPORT.md"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.older", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.TG.parity", "title": "BF21 parity equals black-inner obstruction", "statement": "Identify the even-interior condition of the older contracted graph with the black-inner separator obstruction.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_older-approaches/BRIDGES.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_older-approaches/REPORT.md"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The two conditions belong to different incidence constructions; the radial tree is not H-s.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Truncated-octahedron contraction, author certificate not yet independently replayed.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.older", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "e.census16", "kind": "exhaustive", "tier": "T3", "status": "exhaustive for |V(T)| <= 16: two independent implementations agree instance by instance (no referee yet)", "title": "Census of states, pairs and tree matchings, all rooted Eulerian triangulations with at most 16 vertices", "statement": "7868 rooted triangulations (T, t0), 5088 with a pair. The multiset of (states, pairs, tree matchings) per size is the same in the combinatorics lab (own generator) and in the algebra agent's counts (plantri 4.5 and workings/barnette_lab). Totals: 140358 states, 24744 pairs, 24090 tree matchings. Positive tree-matching counts seen: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16. A third enumeration by the combinatorics referee agrees as well.", "evidence": ["labyrinth/make_frontier.py", "labyrinth/frontier_crosscheck.json", "research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/data/rows_v16.json", "research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/counts.json", "research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/code/"], "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "tests"}, {"to": "k.D.3", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.octahedron", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "Octahedron (dual of the cube), 6 vertices", "statement": "n = 3, 2 states, 2 pairs, 2 tree matchings, cmin = 1. The smallest case; with zero weights Z = i - i = 0.", "links": [{"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "instance-of"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.prism", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "Hexagonal prism dual (hexagonal bipyramid), 8 vertices", "statement": "3 states, 2 pairs, 2 tree matchings. The smallest example that separates: acyclic Q_s from tree matching, the raw determinant from its squarefree coefficient, trinity arborescences from tree matchings, avoiding cycles (4) from recovered cycles (2).", "links": [{"to": "x.R.x1", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x9", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.U.x3", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.A.x1", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.double-octahedron", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "Octahedron glued into a face of an octahedron, 9 vertices", "statement": "The smallest separating triangle. With t0 on the black side: 4 states, 4 pairs, 4 tree matchings, cmin = 2. With t0 on the white side: 4 states, no pair.", "links": [{"to": "th.A.T", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "x.N.x7", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.rarity", "kind": "family", "status": "named family", "title": "q prism duals glued into white faces, 5q + 3 vertices", "statement": "3^q states and 2^q tree matchings: tree matchings are exponentially rare among states.", "links": [{"to": "p.D.5", "rel": "instance-of"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.cls6-12", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3)", "statement": "9 states, 10 pairs, 8 tree matchings. Highest partnered state, all-counterclockwise minimal cover and largest rank difference all fail here; its mirror image gives the lowest-state and clockwise failures.", "links": [{"to": "x.N.x4", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x5", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x6", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.cls158-16", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "16 vertices, class 158, t0 = (2,7,3)", "statement": "A single 13-cycle cover whose two orientations both have a triangle in Q_s. The only failure of 'every cover has a forest orientation' among 5088 rooted cases.", "links": [{"to": "x.N.x3", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.split4", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "Octahedron with every face split in four, 18 vertices (n = 15)", "statement": "20 pairs; the 4 one-cycle pairs all have a cycle in Q_s and the 12 tree pairs all have three cycles. The smallest example found with cyclic Q_s, three D-cycles and one exchange component.", "links": [{"to": "x.N.x3", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.theta26", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "Theta of three cubes-minus-an-edge, 26 vertices", "statement": "2-connected, cubic, bipartite, planar, non-Hamiltonian. 8 states and no pair at every root.", "links": [{"to": "x.S0.x2", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "f.torus3x3", "kind": "family", "status": "named example", "title": "3 x 3 triangular grid on the torus", "statement": "No two induced trees; the dual has 36 Hamiltonian cycles; a root-free pair exists with Q unicyclic.", "links": [{"to": "x.S0.x3", "rel": "supports"}], "tier": null, "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.two-evaluations", "kind": "method", "status": "the one new idea", "title": "A signed sum over pairs, evaluated two ways", "statement": "Fix s and cancel (support on forest pairs); fix D and factor (nonzero at lowest order). Absent from the Barnette literature before 2026.", "links": [{"to": "wp