 functions with no weights (comb, rewritten by its referee), and one integer polynomial F with linear weights 1 + xa, real signs and parity only (dim, refd). The Lean proof uses the second form.", "status": "proved here (1 independent AI referee each; human check pending)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.N.H", "p.N.lin", "th.N.Lean"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-06", "was": "Taylor coefficient of an exponential sum with circulation weights (OpenAI)"}, {"date": "2026-10-18", "was": "integer polynomial per exchange component; marked walk (trees paper)"}, {"date": "2026-10-21", "was": "two sign-reversing involutions on marked objects (Li)"}]}, {"id": "pair", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "Exact hypothesis for the first pair", "result": "A pair exists iff no separating triangle has black inner boundary, iff t0 is on the black side of every separating triangle. One exact Euler identity proves both directions.", "status": "LIT (trees paper Thm 1.2); short proof checked in structure referee INTEGRATION.md; final REPORT still provisional; computed on all 7868 roots up to 16 vertices", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["th.A.T", "p.A.GT", "c.A.c"], "lit": ["trees paper 2026"], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-06", "was": "sufficient: no separating triangle (OpenAI Prop. 3.1)"}, {"date": "2026-11-14", "status": "LIT (trees paper Thm 1.2); short proof proved here (gt, under review); computed on all 7868 roots up to 16 vertices", "was": "A pair exists iff no separating triangle has black inner boundary, iff t0 is on the black side of every separating triangle. One exact Euler identity proves both directions."}]}, {"id": "disk", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "What the disk identity is used for", "result": "Four uses in OpenAI, three in Li. In the real-sign form three uses need only that state cycles are odd; the value 3 is used once.", "status": "proved here (refd, unreviewed)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.C.5", "p.B.0"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-11-14", "was": "four uses of the full identity (dependency-graph audit)"}]}, {"id": "structural", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "Existence proof with no signed count", "result": "None. Eight exact reformulations of the target; every relaxation and every local or extremal rule tested is refuted.", "status": "open; 41 dead ends recorded. Most promising: conjecture k.U.7h (local search from a point-rainbow tree)", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["q.structural", "k.U.7h", "x.U.x5", "x.N.x14"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-11-14", "status": "open; 39 dead ends recorded. Most promising: conjecture k.U.7h (local search from a point-rainbow tree)", "was": "None. Eight exact reformulations of the target; every relaxation and every local or extremal rule tested is refuted."}]}, {"id": "tm-lower", "group": "Structure of tree matchings", "cls": "Lower bound on the number of tree matchings of a rooted triangulation with a pair", "result": "At least 2 cmin, and always even. Conjecture: at least 2^cmin (5088 cases, equality in 4609).", "status": "2 cmin proved here (1 AI referee; human check pending); 2^cmin conjecture", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.D.2", "k.D.3", "e.census16"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-18", "was": "at least 2: both signs occur in every exchange component (trees paper Thm 5.2)"}]}, {"id": "rarity", "group": "Structure of tree matchings", "cls": "Fraction of states that are tree matchings", "result": "Can be (2/3)^q on 5q + 3 vertices: 3^q states, 2^q tree matchings.", "status": "proved here, checked in structure referee INTEGRATION.md Section 6; computed for q <= 6", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.D.5", "f.rarity"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-11-14", "status": "proved here (lim, under review); computed for q <= 6", "was": "Can be (2/3)^q on 5q + 3 vertices: 3^q states, 2^q tree matchings."}]}, {"id": "canonical", "group": "Structure of tree matchings", "cls": "Canonical forest pair", "result": "None known. Highest state, lowest state, one-way minimal cover, largest rank difference, each lattice extreme alone: all refuted. The conjecture campaign reports joint failures of the true minimum and maximum at 18 vertices; independent replay pending.", "status": "reported refuted; finite computation under review", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["k.D.7", "x.N.x4", "x.N.x5", "x.N.x6"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-11-14", "status": "conjecture", "was": "None known. Highest state, lowest state, one-way minimal cover, largest rank difference, each lattice extreme alone: all refuted. 'Lattice minimum or maximum' has no joint failure in 180 random instances."}]}, {"id": "which-hc", "group": "Structure of tree matchings", "cls": "Which Hamiltonian cycles arise from tree matchings", "result": "Exactly the cycles avoiding e0* whose state has a partner. Recovery is injective, not onto (prism: 2 of 4). 3 #TM <= #HC(G).", "status": "proved here (comb: 1 AI referee; lim, gt: under review)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.U.5", "p.F.3", "x.A.x1"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "det", "group": "Formulas and algorithms", "cls": "Determinant formula for Z", "result": "Z = i^(-n) [prod y_t] det(sum_t y_t M_t) with rank-two real blocks; 2^n determinant evaluations. Found independently by four agents; the versions coincide by a gauge through the 3-colouring. No formula without coefficient extraction.", "status": "proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.N.lin", "h.N.1", "x.N.x9", "h.N.4"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-18", "was": "the number of states is |det K_B| (trees paper Lemma 6.1)"}]}, {"id": "algorithm", "group": "Formulas and algorithms", "cls": "Polynomial-time construction of the cycle", "result": "None. Deterministic polynomial space and O(poly(N) 3^(N/4)) time; marked walk 2^O(n log n). Uniform sampling of states is polynomial. The abstract problem without the spoke-graph structure is NP-hard.", "status": "LIT bounds (trees paper); NP-hardness proved here modulo a cited theorem (gt, under review)", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["th.N.T2", "p.ST.4", "x.U.x5", "h.D.8"], "lit": ["trees paper 2026"], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "frontier", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Verified range of the counts", "result": "All rooted Eulerian triangulations with at most 16 vertices: states, pairs and tree matchings agree between two independent implementations (7868 roots); a third recount by a referee agrees.", "status": "exhaustive (T3; no referee of the comparison itself)", "kind": "exhaustive", "refs": ["e.census16"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-11-14", "was": "77 rooted runs, 55 triangulations up to 14 vertices (route-constructive)"}]}, {"id": "formal", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Formal verification", "result": "The upstream Lean proof builds locally (Lean 4.34.1); axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. It proves the conjecture as usually stated, by a route that differs from the paper in four places. Not formalised: Corollary 7.2, Theorem 2.2.", "status": "computed (lean-formalisation, unreviewed)", "kind": "computed", "refs": ["c.G2.c", "th.G2.2"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-10", "was": "third-party report of a kernel replay (cert-machine), not reproduced here"}]}, {"id": "review", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Review state of the proofs written in this project", "result": "AI-refereed: route-combinatorics (FOLLOWS with corrections), determinant claims of route-constructive and route-dimers (CORRECT). Under review: route-graph-theory, limits. Unreviewed: dependency-graph, machinery-literature, route-algebra, route-topology, route-categorical, lean-formalisation, the referees' own additions. Human-checked: none.", "status": "partial", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["q.human"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "hypotheses", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Which hypotheses are needed", "result": "Each one, with a witness: K4 (bipartite), theta of cubes on 26 vertices (3-connected), triangular bipyramid radial graph (cubic), 3 x 3 torus (sphere).", "status": "proved here and computed (lim, under review)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["x.S0.x1", "x.S0.x2", "x.S0.x3"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "new-presentations", "updated": "2026-11-14", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "Additional manuscript routes", "result": "Primal proof, draft A heights proof, draft B scalar-height-moment proof; exact prism families as a separate structural route.", "status": "Proofs supplied; draft A referee reports sentence repairs; remaining independent reviews pending.", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["p.G2.primal", "p.G2.drafta", "p.G2.draftb", "p.D.families"], "lit": [], "previous": []}]}, "summary": {"by_tier": {"T1": 10, "T2": 98, "T3": 1, "T4": 10, "T5": 18, "T6": 25}, "conjectures_open": 18, "conjectures_modified": 0, "deadends": 41, "questions_open": 12, "hunches_live": 25, "under_review": 7, "resolved_by_size": {"6": 1.0, "8": 1.0, "9": 1.0, "10": 1.0, "11": 1.0, "12": 1.0, "13": 1.0, "14": 1.0, "15": 1.0, "16": 1.0, "17": 0.0923, "18": 0.0536, "23": 0.0034, "28": 0.0002, "33": 0.0}}}
