 "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.B.4", "title": "Grinberg count made rigid by a matching", "statement": "3(B - W) = 2l - h is a Grinberg balance in the dual; the bijection adds B = I + l.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/WHAT-WAS-HARD.md 2"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Places the one new lemma next to the oldest tool of the subject.", "test": "State Grinberg's formula for the dual disk and compare term by term.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.hist", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.B.5", "title": "Gauss-Bonnet form for any cycle", "statement": "For a state s and a simple cycle C avoiding the roots, B - W = 2m - h + 2, with m the boundary vertices whose matched face lies inside. The topology agent reports the orientation-free form W = B + 1 as proved (B.6); the status of this exact formula is in topo/ROUTES.md.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P2"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Outcome pending in topo/ROUTES.md.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.C.O", "title": "phase i^J", "statement": "J = (1/3) sum of delta(r(t), s(t)) is an integer; both reversals change J by 2.", "where": ["O (5.1), Lemma 5.2"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.C.L", "title": "(-1)^cw from local turns", "statement": "cw' = #clockwise - #counterclockwise cycles. cw' = -J (dep/correspondence.md 3.1).", "where": ["L Lemmas 16, 17, Claim 26"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.C.T", "title": "epsilon = (-1)^((n+J)/2)", "statement": "A real sign; moves (a) and (b) flip it.", "where": ["T Lemma 4.2, (8)"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.1", "title": "the three signs agree up to a constant", "statement": "i^J = i^(-n) epsilon, and Z(x) = i^(-n) times the sum of T's polynomials over exchange components.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.2", "title": "J is an integer by the 3-colouring alone", "statement": "3J = sum c(s(t)) - sum c(r(t)) = 0 mod 3 because r and s are bijections. J is clockwise minus counterclockwise cycles of D, the total colour winding.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md B0; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.3", "title": "the sign is a Leibniz sign", "statement": "After a gauge by the 3-colouring the sign of a pair is the product of the local turns delta, the sign of a term in an incidence determinant. The real sign is prod_t delta(r(t), s(t)).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.C.x1", "title": "sign as a product of two dimer weights", "statement": "Write the local phase as alpha(r(t)) beta(s(t)) and get Z as a product of two incidence determinants.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "At a face with three non-root corners the two cyclic triple products of the phase have ratio -1, and any separated weight gives ratio 1. Disjointness of r and s is what stops the sum from being one determinant.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: One black triangle with three non-root corners.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.C.4", "title": "height-function form of J", "statement": "The Q_s-reversal can change the cycle structure of D completely and J still moves by exactly 2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C2"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Suggests J(r, s) = g(s) - g(r) plus a term local to Q_s, like a dimer height.", "test": "Fit g on the enumerated pairs of the n = 15 and n = 23 examples.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.K.O", "title": "involution: reverse a cycle of Q_s", "statement": "Cycles of Q_s are directed by r. Reversing one chosen from s alone changes r, keeps the weight and flips the sign. T classifies all components: the number of partners is 0 or 2^k.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.2; L iota_1; T beta, Prop. 2.1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.1", "title": "twisted incidence determinant of Q_s", "statement": "For fixed s the partner sum is kappa det N_s, where N_s is the incidence matrix of Q_s reduced at the roots. It vanishes exactly when Q_s has a cycle. Lemma 5.2 is 'the rows of an incidence matrix around a cycle are dependent'.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C1; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Prop. 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.K.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.2", "title": "support of the multivariate polynomial", "statement": "With one variable per incidence, F(w) has coefficient +1 or -1 on each tree matching and 0 on every other state. So CT F(w)F(1/w) is the number of tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x12", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.3", "title": "quartic Berezin integral", "statement": "F(w) is a two-species Grassmann integral with one quartic term per black face. It has an exact Gaussian decoupling, with no assured sign.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.K.c", "title": "checked on every cyclic second state", "statement": "Every state with a cycle in Q_s has zero signed partner sum; the partner count is 2^k or 0 on 140358 states (comb/lab/extra2.py 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.K.x1", "title": "choose the cycle using r", "statement": "Let the reversed cycle depend on the partner.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (disk identity and bijectivity)"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The reversal changes r, so a rule that reads r need not pick the same cycle on the way back. The choice must be a function of s. No smallest counterexample was searched.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: none recorded; the argument is a proof that the involution property can fail, not an instance", "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.O", "title": "Taylor coefficient of order cmin", "statement": "Unit circulations from dual paths, a slide of edges onto spokes, Z(x) = sum over D of prod (-i e^{xL+} + i e^{xL-}); the coefficient of x^cmin is a nonzero multiple of a positive sum.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.3, (5.3)-(5.5)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.L", "title": "second involution on marked objects", "statement": "Weights are signed crossings of vertical rays. A sign-reversing involution on lists of cmin marks; its fixed points share a sign. For cmin > 1 three verifications are left to the reader (dep/audit-li.md).", "where": ["L Section 4, Defs 14, 20-23, Appendix B"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T1", "title": "integer polynomial per exchange component", "statement": "Integer weights 0 <= a <= 6n; Z_C(z) = sum eps z^omega has a nonzero coefficient of (z - 1)^m. Every exchange component contains tree pairs of both signs.", "where": ["T Lemma 5.1, Thm 5.2, (11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T2", "title": "marked walk (Garsia-Milne)", "statement": "Alternate the two involutions on tokens; the walk ends at a tree pair or restarts with fewer D-cycles. Never computes cmin. 2^O(n log n) time.", "where": ["T Thm 5.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.H", "title": "heights as test functions, no weights", "statement": "Test the signed measure against a product of cmin heights at white faces. Pairs with one D form a cube, partners of one s form a cube, and the product is a cmin-fold difference that survives only on covers with exactly cmin cycles.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Sections 2-3 (Theorem B); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REWRITTEN-PROP-5-1.md (self-contained rewrite by the referee)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x7", "rel": "refutes"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.lin", "title": "linear weights 1 + x a", "statement": "Replace e^{xa} by 1 + xa. The polynomial has degree at most n and the same leading coefficient; on the forest side it is a signed elementary symmetric moment. The Lean proof uses the same polynomial (lean/DIFFERENCES.md item 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 7; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/SIGNIFICANCE.md Section 2 (full proof with real signs and parity only)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.id", "title": "spoke weights are a height function", "statement": "omega(s) is the volume under the height of s, and L+(C) - L-(C) is the number of white faces inside C, which is B + 1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 2.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.N.c", "title": "leading coefficient checked exactly", "statement": "The first nonzero coefficient equals the signed sum of products of enclosed face counts on every instance tested.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/supplemental.py (49 groups); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/code/linear.py; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 5 (71224 rooted triangulations up to 18 vertices)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/supplemental.py (49 groups); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/code/linear.py; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 5 (71224 rooted triangulations up to 18 vertices)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x1", "title": "zero, vertex-only or face-only weights", "statement": "Use weights alpha_t + beta_v, or none.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/data/zero_weights.json; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Such weights are pure gauge: every state has the same total, and the signed count is 0 = 0. What is needed is positive circulation on cycles, not positive weights.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Cube (octahedron dual, 6 vertices): two pairs with J = +1 and -1, Z = i - i = 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x2", "title": "parity or mod p count without weights", "statement": "Show the number of tree matchings is odd, or nonzero mod p.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 8; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/TABLES.md (residues mod 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The number of tree matchings is always even (the two signs balance), and T = P - 2 N_1 mod 4 is compatible with T = 0. The weighted sum is the refinement that works; the first degree at which anything survives is cmin. No modulus among 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11 gives a universally nonzero residue; the positive counts seen are 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 22.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Octahedron: 2 tree matchings, signed count 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x3", "title": "tree pair among the fewest-cycle pairs", "statement": "Among the pairs with the fewest D-cycles one has Q_s a forest; or every cycle cover D has a forest orientation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D2; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 7 (E2d, E3); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md O3 (a 40-vertex one-cycle cover with no tree pair)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Reversals inside one fixed cycle cover cannot be guaranteed to reach a forest pair, so a proof must move between covers. The leading coefficient is nonzero because of the fewest-cycle covers, but the surviving pairs can live in other covers. A statement that held on 1794 cases failed at the next size. (Scope as corrected by the referee.)", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 16 vertices, class 158, t0 = (2,7,3): a single 13-cycle whose two orientations both have a triangle in Q_s; its 12 tree matchings lie in two other covers. Also the octahedron with every face split in four (n = 15).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x4", "title": "highest or lowest partnered state", "statement": "The top (bottom) partnered state of the lattice is a tree matching.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 4 (E1, E1c); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md O1 (extremes of the whole matching lattice fail at 10 vertices)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "For an extreme s every D has all cycles one way, but reversing a cycle of Q_s changes the number of D-cycles by two and extremality does not forbid it.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3) for the highest state, and its mirror image for the lowest (the referee's correction: the author's enumeration identified reflections and reported 14).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x5", "title": "minimal cover, all cycles one way", "statement": "Take D with cmin cycles and orient all of them counterclockwise (or clockwise).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 5 (E2, E2c); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The leading coefficient sums over all minimal covers and prefers no orientation.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3) for counterclockwise, and its mirror image for clockwise (referee's correction; the author reported 13).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x6", "title": "largest rank difference", "statement": "The pair maximising omega(s) - omega(r) is a forest pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 6 (E5)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Maximality forces the cycles of Q_s to be counterclockwise and nothing more.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x7", "title": "one cycle always suffices", "statement": "cmin = 1, so a first-order argument is enough.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 13"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "cmin reaches 3 without separating triangles (192 of 3374 rooted cases up to 16 vertices) and 4 with them. A first-order argument is not enough and Li's Appendix B is needed. Unboundedness of cmin is not proved.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 9 vertices: octahedron with an octahedron glued into a face, cmin = 2.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x8", "title": "cubes of tree matchings; sign = parity of rank", "statement": "Tree matchings split into cubes of dimension cmin; or eps(s) = (-1)^omega(s) up to a constant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 9, 10"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Z(q)/(q - 1)^cmin can have mixed signs, which refutes a rank-compatible signed cube decomposition. An abstract partition into cubes of dimension cmin is refuted by cardinality (referee).", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Signs: 14 vertices, class 24, face 6, Z = -1 + 2q + q^5 - 2q^6. Cardinality: a 13-vertex instance with 6 tree matchings and cmin = 2 (refc/code/cube_cardinality.json). Sign = parity of rank fails at 8 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x9", "title": "ordinary determinant, all face variables 1", "statement": "Evaluate det(sum_t M_t) with no coefficient extraction.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md, data/exact_determinant.json; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/IDENTITIES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Without extraction a black face can supply two transitions and another none; the extra terms can cancel the answer. Testing only the cube or the octahedron would have hidden this.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual (8 vertices): squarefree coefficient 45/64 at z = 5/4, all-one evaluation 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x10", "title": "allow doubled edges (standard double dimers)", "statement": "Add a diagonal so that r and s may share edges, as in Kenyon's double-dimer determinant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 3; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Nonvanishing becomes too easy: 