ove at every non-tree pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 7"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would turn existence into descent.", "test": "Search for a non-tree local minimum of each candidate on small exchange graphs.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.6", "title": "curved double-dimer connection, Lee-Yang", "statement": "Realise the loop factor -i e^{xL+} + i e^{xL-} as the trace of a non-flat connection.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 15; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 8"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Each loop factor is -2i e^{xm} sinh(x Delta/2); zeros lie on the imaginary axis loop by loop.", "test": "Solve the connection equations on two bipyramids and test trace identities on nested loops.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.7", "title": "LGV after cutting along seams", "statement": "Cut the pair diagram into non-intersecting paths and use a Lindstrom-Gessel-Viennot determinant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 8"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "A fixed path matrix would make the sum a single determinant.", "test": "Do the cut on the cube and on the first instance with two D-cycles.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.8", "title": "abstract valuation theorem", "statement": "Axiomatise: a finite signed cycle system, two involutions, a positive circulation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 17"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would say which planar hypotheses do the work.", "test": "List the axioms and find the first one that fails on a torus or a disk with four roots.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.N.9", "title": "a test function with one sign on all covers", "statement": "There is a test function of s for which every cycle cover contributes with the same sign, so that no minimum over the number of cycles is taken.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md, open question 2"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "On the 479 cases with more than 2^cmin tree matchings (comb/data/rows_v16.json), search low-degree polynomials in the heights.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.10", "title": "flux on a small set of faces", "statement": "Put positive flux only on a set of faces that meets the interior of every feasible D-cycle.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md (economical weights)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Smaller weights, smaller degrees.", "test": "Compute minimum hitting sets of cycle interiors on the enumerated instances.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.D.1", "title": "two evaluations of one sum", "statement": "Supported on forest pairs, and not zero.", "where": ["O Prop. 5.1; L Key Lemma 7; T Thm 5.2"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.2", "title": "at least 2 cmin tree matchings", "statement": "The signed measure on tree matchings kills all polynomials of degree below cmin in the rank, and the two signs are equally frequent.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Corollary 3"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.3", "title": "at least 2^cmin tree matchings", "statement": "Every rooted triangulation with a pair has at least 2^cmin tree matchings. True for all 5088 cases up to 16 vertices; equality in 4609.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 11; labyrinth/scatter.json"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Find a rooted triangulation with a pair and fewer than 2^cmin tree matchings; start at 17 vertices with cmin = 3.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}, {"to": "p.D.2", "rel": "generalizes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.4", "title": "exactly one tree matching is impossible", "statement": "The signed unweighted sum over tree matchings is zero, so their number is even. The cube has two.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2 (after T Thm 5.2)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x2", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.D.5", "title": "tree matchings can be exponentially rare", "statement": "Gluing q hexagonal-prism duals into white faces gives 3^q states and 2^q tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (rarity); code/rarity.py q <= 6; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical/PROOF.md Prop. 6 (states, pairs and tree matchings multiply under insertion into a white face)"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_route-categorical"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.cat", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.U.x3", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.D.6", "title": "a canonical forest pair", "statement": "Under a bijection from states to trinity arborescences, tree matchings have a tree description that singles one out.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md step 3"], "tags": ["step D"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Write the Hine-Kalman bijection on the 12-vertex class 6 example where every extremal rule fails, and look at the images of its 8 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.D", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.1", "title": "prescribed-degree spanning tree of H", "statement": "[y^{d*}] det L_H(y) is the number of tree matchings: a positive coefficient of the tree-degree polynomial. Existence would follow from a support theorem for that polynomial.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 1, 4"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.2", "title": "label-transversal white trees", "statement": "Tree matchings are the spanning trees of the restricted white-face graph whose edge labels use every t and every v once. A doubly squarefree coefficient of a Laplacian determinant counts them, by Cauchy-Binet with all terms nonnegative.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 5; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 3"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.3", "title": "three-matroid intersection", "statement": "A common independent set of size n in two partition matroids and the graphic matroid of opposite edges with the roots identified. Duality maps the triple to a triple of the same kind, so it never becomes a two-matroid problem (gt).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 6; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md Section 1"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC). Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.4", "title": "unique partner: |det K_{B-s}| = 1", "statement": "Zeroing the entries of s in K_B gives a determinant equal to the number of partners up to sign. A tree matching is a state where it is 1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 2 (after T Prop. 2.1)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.5", "title": "tree matchings = partnered Hamiltonian cycles", "statement": "Tree matchings are in bijection with the Hamiltonian cycles avoiding e0* whose state has a partner. So 3 #TM <= #HC(G).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Prop. 7; research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md Thm 7.2 (explicit left inverse; image = partitions with acyclic white parent map)"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_limits, 2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.A.x1", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.U.6", "title": "rooted functional orientations; two-sided hypertrees", "statement": "Two more exact restatements of the target, as an orientation problem and as a simultaneous hypertree realisation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 5, 7"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x1", "title": "matching matroid meets graphic matroid", "statement": "Treat the two endpoint constraints as one matroid and use Edmonds' two-matroid intersection.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 6; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/data/other_candidates.json; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/REFEREE-constructive.md"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Matchings are not a matroid (augmentation fails on K_{2,2}). With only the face partition and the white graphic matroid, the augmenting-path algorithm returns white trees that repeat vertices.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism: 4 of the 6 common bases of the two-matroid relaxation are not states (referee's correction, refd). Larger witness: truncated octahedron, eleven spokes repeating non-roots 3 and 4 (con/data/other_candidates.json).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x2", "title": "unconstrained white spanning trees", "statement": "Every