", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.1h", "title": "support of the tree-degree polynomial", "statement": "Show the target degree vector d* lies in the support of det L_H(y), from plane incidence inequalities.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 2; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P8, P9"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "An unsigned target: no cancellation to explain. If every lattice point of the degree polytope were realised (P9), convexity would finish.", "test": "Enumerate H-trees on the cube and the hexagonal bipyramid; compare the support with the lattice points of its convex hull.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.2h", "title": "spanning-tree parity / matroid parity", "statement": "'Each black centre keeps exactly two of its three spokes' looks like the spanning tree parity problem that Feder and Subi solve in polynomial time for 2- and 3-sided faces.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/REPORT.md (leads); research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 10"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "If it is a matroid parity instance, Lovasz gives a polynomial algorithm, against 3^(N/4).", "test": "Design the gadget for one black centre and two adjacent centres; enumerate feasible parity solutions against partial spoke choices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.hist", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.4h", "title": "Bernardi process, Schnyder woods, blossom trees", "statement": "A canonical tree or orientation of the map might produce a tree matching directly.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 4, 11, 12, 13"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Each theory uses three colours and rooted trees on triangulations, as the target does.", "test": "On the octahedron and the hexagonal bipyramid, test every facewise corner rule for bijectivity on X and for the forest condition.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.5h", "title": "order-theoretic position in the state lattice", "statement": "Outcome (topo): the tree matchings are neither an interval nor an antichain of the clock lattice, and the top and bottom states are often tree matchings. No order-theoretic pattern was found.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P6; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 9"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Decided on the topology agent's sample (166 lattices); a description of the subset is still missing.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.6h", "title": "describe partnered Hamiltonian cycles in G alone", "statement": "There is a description, without states, of the Hamiltonian cycles of G avoiding e0* whose state has a partner.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md, open question 3"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "For the hexagonal prism list the 2 partnered and 2 unpartnered avoiding cycles and compare their face sequences; then test any candidate rule on the 176726 unpartnered cycles of the survey.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.R.1", "title": "out-degree count", "statement": "A tree component with v vertices and a roots has v - a out-edges and v - 1 edges, so a = 1. T: s is a tree matching iff it has exactly one partner.", "where": ["O Lemma 6.1; L Lemma 8; T (3), Prop. 2.1, Thm 1.2"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.R.c", "title": "unique partner checked on 140358 states", "statement": "Brute force over all states: tree matching iff exactly one partner; the partner count is 2^k or 0.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/extra2.py 16; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/extra2.py 16; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.R.x1", "title": "a forest state is enough", "statement": "Call s good as soon as Q_s is acyclic, with no partner assumed.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (forest versus rooted forest); research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.5"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Without the partner the out-degree count is unavailable: a component can hold two roots and another none. 'Forest', 'cycle-breaking' and 'tree matching' agree for pairs and differ for single states.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual: all 3 states have acyclic Q_s, only 2 are tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.E.1", "title": "tree-cotree duality", "statement": "The duals of the deleted spokes form a spanning tree on the white faces.", "where": ["O Lemma 2.1; L Cor. 27; T 7.1"], "tags": ["step E"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.E.2", "title": "Temperley / Kenyon-Propp-Wilson", "statement": "Read the step as the tree-to-matching bijection of KPW.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md E2; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step E"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "KPW applied to the white graph encodes all its spanning trees and carries the label constraints along; it does not identify those dimers with B (dim).", "test": "Write the bijection for the octahedron and the n = 15 example.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.E2.1", "title": "orient towards y0", "statement": "Each tree edge is assigned to its end farther from y0 and selects the side of its black face bordering that end.", "where": ["O 6.1; L Claim 31; T 7.1"], "tags": ["step E2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.E2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.E2.2", "title": "the three papers select the same P", "statement": "Li's trace of the dual tree through black vertices gives the same set of edges of G.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.6"], "tags": ["step E2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established: proved here (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.F.OT", "title": "P is a forest, by the disk identity", "statement": "A cycle in P0 would be directed, and the selected-side count gives a disk with one black face fewer than the state requires. Then duality gives the cycle and the Jordan curve the two induced trees.", "where": ["O Lemma 6.2; T Lemma 7.1"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC"