0 vertices (Brinkmann-Goedgebeur-McKay)"}, {"date": "2025-01-01", "was": "proved for faces of size at most 8 (Schnieders)"}]}, {"id": "prop51", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "Shortest rigorous proof of Proposition 5.1 (a pair implies a forest pair)", "result": "Two candidates of about one page: heights as test functions with no weights (comb, rewritten by its referee), and one integer polynomial F with linear weights 1 + xa, real signs and parity only (dim, refd). The Lean proof uses the second form.", "status": "proved here (1 independent AI referee each; human check pending)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.N.H", "p.N.lin", "th.N.Lean"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-06", "was": "Taylor coefficient of an exponential sum with circulation weights (OpenAI)"}, {"date": "2026-10-18", "was": "integer polynomial per exchange component; marked walk (trees paper)"}, {"date": "2026-10-21", "was": "two sign-reversing involutions on marked objects (Li)"}]}, {"id": "pair", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "Exact hypothesis for the first pair", "result": "A pair exists iff no separating triangle has black inner boundary, iff t0 is on the black side of every separating triangle. One exact Euler identity proves both directions.", "status": "LIT (trees paper Thm 1.2); short proof proved here (gt, under review); computed on all 7868 roots up to 16 vertices", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["th.A.T", "p.A.GT", "c.A.c"], "lit": ["trees paper 2026"], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-06", "was": "sufficient: no separating triangle (OpenAI Prop. 3.1)"}]}, {"id": "disk", "group": "The theorem and its proofs", "cls": "What the disk identity is used for", "result": "Four uses in OpenAI, three in Li. In the real-sign form three uses need only that state cycles are odd; the value 3 is used once.", "status": "proved here (refd, unreviewed)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.C.5", "p.B.0"], "lit": [], "updated": "2