c", "group": "Structure of tree matchings", "cls": "Which Hamiltonian cycles arise from tree matchings", "result": "Exactly the cycles avoiding e0* whose state has a partner. Recovery is injective, not onto (prism: 2 of 4). 3 #TM <= #HC(G).", "status": "proved here (comb: 1 AI referee; lim, gt: under review)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.U.5", "p.F.3", "x.A.x1"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "det", "group": "Formulas and algorithms", "cls": "Determinant formula for Z", "result": "Z = i^(-n) [prod y_t] det(sum_t y_t M_t) with rank-two real blocks; 2^n determinant evaluations. Found independently by four agents; the versions coincide by a gauge through the 3-colouring. No formula without coefficient extraction.", "status": "proved here (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["p.N.lin", "h.N.1", "x.N.x9", "h.N.4"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-18", "was": "the number of states is |det K_B| (trees paper Lemma 6.1)"}]}, {"id": "algorithm", "group": "Formulas and algorithms", "cls": "Polynomial-time construction of the cycle", "result": "None. Deterministic polynomial space and O(poly(N) 3^(N/4)) time; marked walk 2^O(n log n). Uniform sampling of states is polynomial. The abstract problem without the spoke-graph structure is NP-hard.", "status": "LIT bounds (trees paper); NP-hardness proved here modulo a cited theorem (gt, under review)", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["th.N.T2", "p.ST.4", "x.U.x5", "h.D.8"], "lit": ["trees paper 2026"], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "frontier", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Verified range of the counts", "result": "All rooted Eulerian triangulations with at most 16 vertices: states, pairs and tree matchings agree between two independent implementations (7868 roots); a third recount by a referee agrees.", "status": "exhaustive (T3; no referee of the comparison itself)", "kind": "exhaustive", "refs": ["e.census16"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-11-14", "was": "77 rooted runs, 55 triangulations up to 14 vertices (route-constructive)"}]}, {"id": "formal", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Formal verification", "result": "The upstream Lean proof builds locally (Lean 4.34.1); axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. It proves the conjecture as usually stated, by a route that differs from the paper in four places. Not formalised: Corollary 7.2, Theorem 2.2.", "status": "computed (lean-formalisation, unreviewed)", "kind": "computed", "refs": ["c.G2.c", "th.G2.2"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": [{"date": "2026-10-10", "was": "third-party report of a kernel replay (cert-machine), not reproduced here"}]}, {"id": "review", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Review state of the proofs written in this project", "result": "AI-refereed: route-combinatorics (FOLLOWS with corrections), determinant claims of route-constructive and route-dimers (CORRECT). Under review: route-graph-theory, limits. Unreviewed: dependency-graph, machinery-literature, route-algebra, route-topology, route-categorical, lean-formalisation, the referees' own additions. Human-checked: none.", "status": "partial", "kind": "partial", "refs": ["q.human"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}, {"id": "hypotheses", "group": "Verification", "cls": "Which hypotheses are needed", "result": "Each one, with a witness: K4 (bipartite), theta of cubes on 26 vertices (3-connected), triangular bipyramid radial graph (cubic), 3 x 3 torus (sphere).", "status": "proved here and computed (lim, under review)", "kind": "proved", "refs": ["x.S0.x1", "x.S0.x2", "x.S0.x3"], "lit": [], "updated": "2026-11-14", "previous": []}]}, "summary": {"by_tier": {"T1": 62, "T2": 40, "T3": 1, "T4": 9, "T5": 17, "T6": 24}, "conjectures_open": 17, "conjectures_modified": 0, "deadends": 39, "questions_open": 12, "hunches_live": 24, "under_review": 7, "resolved_by_size": {"6": 1.0, "8": 1.