t-B", "statement": "Agent archive paper/draft-B/. Review state of its proofs: unreviewed.", "where": ["paper/draft-B/REPORT.md"], "links": [], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "src.agent.reft", "kind": "source", "tier": null, "status": "agent folder", "title": "2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology", "statement": "Agent archive research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/. Review state of its proofs: unreviewed.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-topology/REPORT.md"], "links": [], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "tags": [], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.G", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Barnette graph G", "statement": "Cubic, bipartite, 3-connected, planar. The claim is that G has a Hamiltonian cycle, and more: one that avoids any prescribed edge.", "links": [], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.T", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Dual Eulerian triangulation (T, t0, e0)", "statement": "T = G* is a simple sphere triangulation with faces coloured black and white. Root it at a black face t0 with an edge e0. Vertices of G are faces of T, faces of G are vertices of T.", "links": [{"to": "wp.G", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.2T", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Two induced trees", "statement": "The goal in dual form. G has a Hamiltonian cycle avoiding e0* if and only if V(T) splits into two sets, each inducing a tree, with both ends of e0 in one of them (Stein 1971; APSW 2016).", "links": [{"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.S", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "States", "statement": "A state is a bijection s from the bounded black faces A to the non-root vertices X with s(t) a corner of t. It is a perfect matching of the incidence graph B. |A| = |X| = n.", "links": [{"to": "wp.T", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.P", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "A pair (r, s)", "statement": "Two states that differ at every face. The partner r is the certificate that orients Q_s: the edge opposite s(t) in t is directed out of r(t).", "links": [{"to": "wp.S", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.DI", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Disk identity", "statement": "A directed cycle of state edges of length h with l black faces of its disk along it has 2l - h = -3. Equivalently its disk holds exactly one more white face than black faces.", "links": [{"to": "wp.T", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.M", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Signed measure on pairs", "statement": "Every pair gets a sign (i^J in O, (-1)^cw in L, epsilon in T). Reversing a cycle of D(r, s) flips it, and reversing a cycle of Q_s flips it. The whole proof is one signed sum over pairs, weighted by a function of s.", "links": [{"to": "wp.P", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.K", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Cancellation of cyclic Q_s", "statement": "Sum with s fixed. If Q_s has a cycle, reversing it changes r, keeps s and the weight, and flips the sign. So only pairs with Q_s a forest survive.", "links": [{"to": "wp.M", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.N", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Nonvanishing", "statement": "Sum with the undirected cycle set D fixed. With weights whose circulation is positive on every counterclockwise spoke cycle, the lowest-order term is a positive count of the covers with fewest cycles.", "links": [{"to": "wp.M", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.FP", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Forest pair / tree matching", "statement": "A pair with Q_s a forest. Equivalently a state s with H - s a spanning tree of the spoke graph. Equivalently a state with exactly one partner.", "links": [{"to": "wp.K", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.IT", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Incidence tree H - s", "statement": "Delete the n matched spokes from the spoke graph H. What is left is a spanning tree: every black centre keeps two spokes, t0 keeps three.", "links": [{"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.WT", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "White-face tree", "statement": "The duals of the n deleted spokes form a spanning tree on the white faces (tree-cotree duality in the plane).", "links": [{"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.SE", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Selected edges P", "statement": "Root the white tree at y0, the white face across e0. Each tree edge selects one side of its black face. With e0 this is one edge in every face of T, a perfect matching of G.", "links": [{"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.JC", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Jordan curve", "statement": "E(G) - P is 2-regular. It is a single cycle, hence a Jordan curve on the sphere, and its two sides are the two induced trees.", "links": [{"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.GL", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Gluing", "statement": "If a separating triangle blocks the state method at this root, cut along it, cap both sides, solve each with the cap edge prescribed, and glue.", "links": [{"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "wp.HC", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "review": {"state": "unreviewed"}, "status": "source waypoint; unrefereed preprint, not a peer-review claim", "title": "Hamiltonian cycle", "statement": "Every Barnette graph has a Hamiltonian cycle avoiding any prescribed edge (O Theorem 1.1, Corollary 7.1).", "links": [{"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "uses"}], "tags": ["waypoint"], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.S0", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step S0: Dualise and root", "statement": "3-connected cubic plane graphs are the duals of simple triangulations, and bipartite means the faces of T 2-colour. This is the only place 3-connectivity is used.", "note": "No freedom in the statement. Li keeps the primal language through the auxiliary graph aux(G); the objects are the same.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.G", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.T", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.TG", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step TG: Restate the goal", "statement": "A Hamiltonian cycle of G is a Jordan curve; the faces of G on each side are vertices of T inducing a tree. Known since Stein. All pre-2026 attacks tried to cross here directly.", "note": "This is the edge that 57 years of partial results worked on. None of them reaches all Barnette graphs.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.T", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.ST", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step ST: Define states and count", "statement": "Euler's formula gives equally many black and white faces k and k + 2 vertices, so |A| = |X| = k - 1. Without this equality there is nothing to match.", "note": "States are Tutte's trinity states with the colours swapped. Their number is a determinant.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.T", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.A", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "free", "title": "Step A: Find two disjoint states", "statement": "The incidence graph B must contain two edge-disjoint perfect matchings. This is where a separating triangle can obstruct, and the only place the papers use 'no separating triangle'.", "note": "Four published arguments (flow with a density bound; Ore deficiency with a minimal set; the exact criterion; Hall on a gadget in the Lean proof). They prove different amounts.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.S", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.B", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step B: Prove the disk identity", "statement": "Euler's formula on the disk, a signed count of sides, and B = I + l, which holds because a state is a bijection.", "note": "One double count in all three papers, on triangles (O, T) or on hexagons of the spoke graph (L). A second derivation, as the theorem of turning tangents for an angle structure, is proved in the topology folder and unreviewed.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.T", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.C", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step C: Sign the pairs", "statement": "Define the sign and show that both reversals flip it. The disk identity is used twice here: on the cycles of D and on the cycle of Q_s.", "note": "Three notations for one sign. The complex phase is packaging; a real sign is enough.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.P", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.K", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step K: Cancel with s fixed", "statement": "The reversed cycle of Q_s must be chosen from s alone, so that the map is an involution that keeps the weight.", "note": "All three papers use the same involution. It is the statement that a twisted incidence determinant of Q_s vanishes on a cycle.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.M", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.N", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "free", "title": "Step N: Show the total is not zero", "statement": "Weights that depend on s only and separate the two orientations of every D-cycle. Then group by D and find a term that cannot cancel.", "note": "The widest step: five published arguments, two more proved here, and a long list of refuted shortcuts. Every route that works still minimises over the number of cycles.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.M", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.D", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step D: Compare the two evaluations", "statement": "The same sum is supported on forest pairs (by K) and is not zero (by N). So a forest pair exists.", "note": "The comparison is one line. No canonical forest pair is known: every extremal choice tried is refuted.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.K", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.U", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "open", "title": "Step U: Unsigned routes (bypass)", "statement": "Find a tree matching with no signed sum: as a prescribed-degree spanning tree, a three-matroid intersection, a constrained white tree, a point of the state lattice.", "note": "Many exact reformulations are proved. None has an existence argument. Every relaxation tried drops a constraint and is refuted by a small example.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.S", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.R", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step R: One root per component", "statement": "The partner gives out-degree one at non-roots and zero at roots, so a tree component of Q_s has exactly one root. With the three spokes of t0 this makes H - s a spanning tree.", "note": "Same count in all three papers. A forest without a partner is not enough.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.E", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "rigid", "title": "Step E: Tree-cotree duality", "statement": "The complement of a spanning tree of a plane graph is a spanning tree of the dual.", "note": "Rigid as a statement. The Lean proof skips the node: it selects P inside G and never builds the white tree.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.E2", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "rigid", "title": "Step E2: Root at y0 and select", "statement": "Orient the white tree towards y0; the edge above each white face selects one side of a black face.", "note": "Rigid. The three papers select the same set P.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.F", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "free", "title": "Step F: Show P leaves one cycle", "statement": "P has one edge in every face of T, so E(G) - P is 2-regular. It must be connected.", "note": "Two published arguments. O, T and the Lean proof count against the disk identity (a third use). Li uses an innermost cycle and needs neither the disk identity nor the partner.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.J2", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step J2: Sides of the curve", "statement": "The two sides of the Jordan curve are the two induced trees, and e0 lies in one of them.", "note": "Li skips this node and glues Hamiltonian cycles directly.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.G", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step G: Cut at separating triangles", "statement": "The prescribed edge is what lets two solutions agree on the cap. An unbounded prescription would be NP-hard.", "note": "Same induction in all three papers, known since Kelmans 1986. The trees paper cuts less often.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "m.step.G2", "kind": "method", "tier": null, "status": "forced", "title": "Step G2: Conclude", "statement": "Induction on the number of vertices, or a minimum counterexample.", "note": "None.", "tags": ["step"], "links": [{"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "uses"}, {"to": "wp.HC", "rel": "supports"}], "where": ["digestions/route-map/ROUTE-MAP.md"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.S0.1", "title": "duality; 3-connectivity gives a simple T", "statement": "The dual of a 3-connected cubic plane graph is a simple triangulation; G bipartite iff T Eulerian iff the faces of T 2-colour iff the vertices 3-colour.", "where": ["O proof of Thm 1.1; APSW 2016 Section 1"], "tags": ["step S0"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.S0", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.S0.2", "title": "stay in G with aux(G)", "statement": "Li works in the primal graph with the face/black-vertex incidence graph. aux(G) is T with a centre in every face.", "where": ["L Section 2"], "tags": ["step S0"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.S0", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.S0.3", "title": "3-connectivity enters only here", "statement": "In O, 3-connectivity is used once, to exclude loops and parallel edges in the dual. Simplicity is then used in the flow bound and the gluing.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/audit-openai.md, REPORT.md"], "tags": ["step S0"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.S0", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.S0.x1", "title": "drop bipartite", "statement": "Without bipartiteness there is no proper face colouring of T, so states are not defined.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; examples/K4.json, Tutte46.json"], "tags": ["step S0"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Odd degrees obstruct the algebra itself, before any question of Hamiltonicity. Best max-cut colourings of K4, BBL38 and Tutte's graph leave 2, 7 and 9 monochromatic adjacencies.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: K4 (4 vertices): the dual has all degrees odd. Tutte's 46-vertex graph is the non-Hamiltonian witness.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.S0", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.S0.x2", "title": "drop 3-connectivity", "statement": "A 2-connected cubic bipartite planar graph can be non-Hamiltonian. Its dual has parallel edges.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; examples/theta_cube_26.json"], "tags": ["step S0"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The proof stops at the pair: the 26-vertex theta of three cubes-minus-an-edge has 8 states and no disjoint pair at each of its 26 roots. The disk identity itself survives in the multimap.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: theta of three copies of cube-minus-edge, 26 vertices (minimum by Asano-Saito-Exoo-Harary 1982, abstract only).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.S0", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.S0.x3", "title": "other surfaces", "statement": "On an orientable surface of genus g, |A| - |X| = 2g, so states with three roots do not exist for g > 0, and the two-tree target is impossible on the torus by an edge count.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; examples/torus_3x3.json"], "tags": ["step S0"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The first obstruction is cardinality. A surface version needs a different state and a different target (one edge per triangle with connected complementary dual).", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 3 x 3 periodic triangular grid on the torus: no two induced trees, yet the dual has 36 Hamiltonian cycles.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.S0", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.TG.1", "title": "Stein 1971; APSW Lemma 5", "statement": "T* is Hamiltonian iff V(T) splits into two induced forests, which for triangulations are two induced trees.", "where": ["Stein, Pacific J. Math. 37 (1971), Thm 2.2; APSW 2016, Lemma 5"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.TG.2", "title": "prescribed edge: O Theorem 2.2", "statement": "With e0 inside one tree the cycle avoids e0*. This is the H- form of Kelmans and Hertel, equivalent to the conjecture.", "where": ["O Thm 2.2; research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/EQUIVALENTS.md 9, 14a"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.TG.3", "title": "face-size results (Goodey; Schnieders)", "statement": "Hamiltonicity when all faces have size at most 6 (Goodey), at most 8 (Schnieders, 339 million computer cases). Partial: local reductions cannot see 3-connectivity, which becomes necessary at face size 10.", "where": ["Goodey 1975; Feder-Subi 2006; Schnieders 2025 (research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/RESULTS-TABLE.md)"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published), partial result", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.TG.4", "title": "computer search to 90 vertices", "statement": "All Barnette graphs up to 90 vertices are Hamiltonian.", "where": ["Brinkmann-Goedgebeur-McKay, Math. Comp. 2022"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published), partial result", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.TG.5", "title": "trees of faces (Feder-Subi)", "statement": "Contract a colour class of faces and look for a quasi spanning tree of faces. Polynomial when the remaining faces have 2 or 3 sides, NP-complete in general. The closest older relative of the incidence tree.", "where": ["Feder-Subi 2006; Bagheri Gh. et al. 2021"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published), partial result", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.TG.6", "title": "A-trails, braces, book embeddings", "statement": "Equivalent formulations in other languages. None supplied an existence mechanism.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/EQUIVALENTS.md 6, 11, 12"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published), partial result", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.TG.x1", "title": "trees from colour classes", "statement": "Build a permeating subtree containing all or none of a colour class of the vertex 3-colouring.", "where": ["APSW 2016 (limitation theorem); research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/WHAT-WAS-HARD.md 5"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "APSW give Eulerian triangulations in which every permeating subtree contains at least k and misses at least k vertices of every colour class. The trees of the 2026 proofs come from a matching, not from colour classes.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: APSW 2016, family for every k (not reconstructed here).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.TG.x2", "title": "Grinberg obstruction", "statement": "Use Grinberg's formula with a modulus to decide Hamiltonicity.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/WHAT-WAS-HARD.md 2; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/PROOFS.md (Grinberg's identity is automatic for two induced trees)"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "A Barnette graph has f_4 = 6 + sum (k/2 - 3) f_k, so at least six faces of weight 2 and the classical modulus argument cannot apply. PROVED-HERE in the history folder.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Any Barnette graph: at least six 4-faces.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.hist", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.TG.h1", "title": "induced-forest completion", "statement": "Start from a large induced forest and exchange vertices until both sides are trees.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 18"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Farthest from the pair machinery. The general Albertson-Berman conjecture cannot be an input: 2026 preprints report counterexamples.", "test": "Enumerate maximum induced forests on small Eulerian triangulations and look for a trapped configuration.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.TG.h2", "title": "nodal domains of eigenvectors", "statement": "Sign patterns of Laplacian eigenvectors of T almost never give two induced trees (predicted below 5 per cent).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P10"], "tags": ["step TG"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Run over the sample of the topology agent; outcome pending in topo/ROUTES.md.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.TG", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.2T", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.ST.1", "title": "Euler count |A| = |X|", "statement": "k black faces, k white faces, k + 2 vertices, so n = k - 1 on both sides of B.", "where": ["O (2.1); T (2); L omits it"], "tags": ["step ST"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.ST", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.ST.2", "title": "states = trinity states; number = |det K_B|", "statement": "All states have one permutation sign, so their number is |det K_B|, Tutte's magic number, the number of arborescences of each of the three trinity graphs.", "where": ["T Lemma 6.1; Hine-Kalman 2018 Thm 4.3, Lemma 4.4 (research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md)"], "tags": ["step ST"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.ST", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.ST.3", "title": "states form a distributive lattice", "statement": "Clock moves connect all states. The tree matchings are a subset of this lattice with no known description.", "where": ["Hine-Kalman 2018 (clock theorem); research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 9"], "tags": ["step ST"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.ST", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.ST.4", "title": "uniform sampling of states", "statement": "Because all extensions of a partial matching have one sign, residual determinants count them, and a state can be sampled uniformly in polynomial time. This does not sample tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md"], "tags": ["step ST"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.ST", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.S", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.A.O", "title": "max-flow + planar density bound", "statement": "No separating triangle implies the Hall-type condition for two disjoint matchings, by bounding every component of T[U].", "where": ["O Prop. 3.1, (3.1)-(3.4)"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.A.L", "title": "Ore deficiency, minimal deficient set", "statement": "A minimal deficient set yields a non-trivial 3-edge cut. The balance |B'| = |F'| needed for Ore is not stated in the note.", "where": ["L Lemma 9, Theorem 10 (Ore), Claim 12"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.A.T", "title": "exact criterion: no black-inner separating triangle", "statement": "A pair exists if and only if t0 lies on the black side of every separating triangle.", "where": ["T Thm 1.2 (ii) iff (iii), Section 3"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.R.x1", "rel": "refutes"}, {"to": "th.A.O", "rel": "generalizes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.A.c", "title": "criterion checked on all roots to 16 vertices", "statement": "Pair existence agrees with absence of a black-inner separating triangle at every root tested.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/code/campaign.py 14 (1206 roots); research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md (77 runs); gt (all 7868 rooted instances up to 16 vertices against max-flow)"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/code/campaign.py 14 (1206 roots); research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md (77 runs); gt (all 7868 rooted instances up to 16 vertices against max-flow)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.A.d", "title": "Li's Lemma 9 already gives the black inner boundary", "statement": "For a minimal deficient set all three cut edges have their black end inside, so Li's proof gives (iii) implies (ii) of T Theorem 1.2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.7"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.A.1", "title": "induction over local expansions", "statement": "Grow rooted Eulerian triangulations by vertex splits and show a pair survives each split.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md A1"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would replace the flow argument by a local rule.", "test": "For each expansion look for a local map from pairs to pairs; check on all pairs for n <= 15.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.A.x1", "title": "every avoiding cycle comes from a tree matching", "statement": "If every Hamiltonian cycle avoiding e0* came from a tree matching, known Hamiltonicity results would give pairs with no flow argument.", "where": ["posed in research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md A2; refuted by research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 12 (E8) and research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/examples/prism_recovery.json"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The recovery map is injective and not onto. A cycle avoiding e0* always defines a state, and that state is a tree matching or has no partner at all. Most avoiding cycles are of the second kind (ratio up to 26).", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism (dual with 8 vertices): 4 cycles avoid the edge, 2 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.A.3", "title": "matroid union", "statement": "Two disjoint matchings as a basis of a union of transversal matroids.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md A3"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Expected to reduce to the same deficiency count. Recorded so nobody spends an afternoon on it.", "test": "Write the rank formula and compare with O (3.1).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.A.2", "title": "roots not on a common face", "statement": "For every simple 2-coloured triangulation some triple of roots of three colours, not necessarily the corners of a face, admits two disjoint states. The categorical agent tested the two-root version: the obstruction moves and the recovery lemma fails without a root face (A.x2).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md G2"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "On the smallest black-inner example (9 vertices, lim/examples/t9_0.json, outer face 2) enumerate all root triples and count pairs.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.A.4", "title": "pair counts depend on the root", "statement": "In plantri graph 12_2 one black root has 9 states, 10 pairs, 8 tree matchings; every other black root has 9, 2, 2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/data/roots.json"], "tags": ["step A"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/data/roots.json"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.A", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.P", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.B.O", "title": "Euler + side count + bijection, on triangles", "statement": "B + W = 2I + h - 2, 3(B - W) = 2l - h and B = I + l give 2l - h = -3. T adds that the length is odd.", "where": ["O Lemma 4.1, (4.1), (4.2); T Lemma 4.1"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.B.L", "title": "the same count on hexagons of the spoke graph", "statement": "t_in = |C|/4 - 3/2 for an alternating cycle of the spoke graph. Same identity with t_in = l (dep/correspondence.md 3.2).", "where": ["L Claim 25"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.B.0", "title": "reading: W = B + 1, degree -1 of the colouring", "statement": "With the vertex 3-colouring c, delta(v, w) = c(w) - c(v) mod 3. The identity says the disk of a directed state cycle holds one more white face than black faces; the colouring map has degree -1 on it.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md B0; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Section 1"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep"