e hexagons, 6 = 2 mod 4, which is Kasteleyn's condition. The common sign of all states uses only the parity part of the disk identity.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md B1"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "The disk identity may be a flatness condition for a Z/4 or complex signing of spokes.", "test": "Derive t_out - t_in = 3 from a flatness condition for such a signing.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.B.2", "title": "discrete Morse theory", "statement": "Read the state as a pairing of black faces with vertices in the disk and compute the degree from the unpaired cells.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md B2"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "B = I + l looks like a cancellation of cells.", "test": "Write the pairing as a discrete vector field and check that one white face is always left over.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.B.3", "title": "peel the disk", "statement": "Remove a boundary vertex with its matched black face and show 2l - h does not change.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md B3"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "An inductive proof with a picture per step.", "test": "Implement the peeling on enumerated cycles.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.B.4", "title": "Grinberg count made rigid by a matching", "statement": "3(B - W) = 2l - h is a Grinberg balance in the dual; the bijection adds B = I + l.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/WHAT-WAS-HARD.md 2"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Places the one new lemma next to the oldest tool of the subject.", "test": "State Grinberg's formula for the dual disk and compare term by term.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.hist", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.B.5", "title": "Gauss-Bonnet form for any cycle", "statement": "For a state s and a simple cycle C avoiding the roots, B - W = 2m - h + 2, with m the boundary vertices whose matched face lies inside. The topology agent reports the orientation-free form W = B + 1 as proved (B.6); the status of this exact formula is in topo/ROUTES.md.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P2"], "tags": ["step B"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Outcome pending in topo/ROUTES.md.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.B", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.DI", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.C.O", "title": "phase i^J", "statement": "J = (1/3) sum of delta(r(t), s(t)) is an integer; both reversals change J by 2.", "where": ["O (5.1), Lemma 5.2"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.C.L", "title": "(-1)^cw from local turns", "statement": "cw' = #clockwise - #counterclockwise cycles. cw' = -J (dep/correspondence.md 3.1).", "where": ["L Lemmas 16, 17, Claim 26"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.C.T", "title": "epsilon = (-1)^((n+J)/2)", "statement": "A real sign; moves (a) and (b) flip it.", "where": ["T Lemma 4.2, (8)"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.1", "title": "the three signs agree up to a constant", "statement": "i^J = i^(-n) epsilon, and Z(x) = i^(-n) times the sum of T's polynomials over exchange components.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.2", "title": "J is an integer by the 3-colouring alone", "statement": "3J = sum c(s(t)) - sum c(r(t)) = 0 mod 3 because r and s are bijections. J is clockwise minus counterclockwise cycles of D, the total colour winding.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md B0; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.C.3", "title": "the sign is a Leibniz sign", "statement": "After a gauge by the 3-colouring the sign of a pair is the product of the local turns delta, the sign of a term in an incidence determinant. The real sign is prod_t delta(r(t), s(t)).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.C.x1", "title": "sign as a product of two dimer weights", "statement": "Write the local phase as alpha(r(t)) beta(s(t)) and get Z as a product of two incidence determinants.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "At a face with three non-root corners the two cyclic triple products of the phase have ratio -1, and any separated weight gives ratio 1. Disjointness of r and s is what stops the sum from being one determinant.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: One black triangle with three non-root corners.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.C.4", "title": "height-function form of J", "statement": "The Q_s-reversal can change the cycle structure of D completely and J still moves by exactly 2.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C2"], "tags": ["step C"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Suggests J(r, s) = g(s) - g(r) plus a term local to Q_s, like a dimer height.", "test": "Fit g on the enumerated pairs of the n = 15 and n = 23 examples.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.C", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.M", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.K.O", "title": "involution: reverse a cycle of Q_s", "statement": "Cycles of Q_s are directed by r. Reversing one chosen from s alone changes r, keeps the weight and flips the sign. T classifies all components: the number of partners is 0 or 2^k.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.2; L iota_1; T beta, Prop. 2.1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.1", "title": "twisted incidence determinant of Q_s", "statement": "For fixed s the partner sum is kappa det N_s, where N_s is the incidence matrix of Q_s reduced at the roots. It vanishes exactly when Q_s has a cycle. Lemma 5.2 is 'the rows of an incidence matrix around a cycle are dependent'.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md C1; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Prop. 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.K.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.2", "title": "support of the multivariate polynomial", "statement": "With one variable per incidence, F(w) has coefficient +1 or -1 on each tree matching and 0 on every other state. So CT F(w)F(1/w) is the number of tree matchings.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x12", "rel": "refutes"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.K.3", "title": "quartic Berezin integral", "statement": "F(w) is a two-species Grassmann integral with one quartic term per black face. It has an exact Gaussian decoupling, with no assured sign.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 5"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.K.c", "title": "checked on every cyclic second state", "statement": "Every state with a cycle in Q_s has zero signed partner sum; the partner count is 2^k or 0 on 140358 states (comb/lab/extra2.py 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/scripts/check_nodes.py (35 cases); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.K", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.K.x1", "title": "choose the cycle using r", "statement": "Let the reversed cycle depend on the partner.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (disk identity and bijectivity)"], "tags": ["step K"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The reversal changes r, so a rule that reads r need not pick the same cycle on the way back. The choice must be a function of s. No smallest counterexample was searched.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: none recorded; the argument is a proof that the involution property can fail, not an instance", "links": [{"to": "m.step.K", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.O", "title": "Taylor coefficient of order cmin", "statement": "Unit circulations from dual paths, a slide of edges onto spokes, Z(x) = sum over D of prod (-i e^{xL+} + i e^{xL-}); the coefficient of x^cmin is a nonzero multiple of a positive sum.", "where": ["O Lemma 5.3, (5.3)-(5.5)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.L", "title": "second involution on marked objects", "statement": "Weights are signed crossings of vertical rays. A sign-reversing involution on lists of cmin marks; its fixed points share a sign. For cmin > 1 three verifications are left to the reader (dep/audit-li.md).", "where": ["L Section 4, Defs 14, 20-23, Appendix B"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T1", "title": "integer polynomial per exchange component", "statement": "Integer weights 0 <= a <= 6n; Z_C(z) = sum eps z^omega has a nonzero coefficient of (z - 1)^m. Every exchange component contains tree pairs of both signs.", "where": ["T Lemma 5.1, Thm 5.2, (11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.N.T2", "title": "marked walk (Garsia-Milne)", "statement": "Alternate the two involutions on tokens; the walk ends at a tree pair or restarts with fewer D-cycles. Never computes cmin. 2^O(n log n) time.", "where": ["T Thm 5.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.H", "title": "heights as test functions, no weights", "statement": "Test the signed measure against a product of cmin heights at white faces. Pairs with one D form a cube, partners of one s form a cube, and the product is a cmin-fold difference that survives only on covers with exactly cmin cycles.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Sections 2-3 (Theorem B); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REWRITTEN-PROP-5-1.md (self-contained rewrite by the referee)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "x.N.x7", "rel": "refutes"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.lin", "title": "linear weights 1 + x a", "statement": "Replace e^{xa} by 1 + xa. The polynomial has degree at most n and the same leading coefficient; on the forest side it is a signed elementary symmetric moment. The Lean proof uses the same polynomial (lean/DIFFERENCES.md item 16).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 7; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/SIGNIFICANCE.md Section 2 (full proof with real signs and parity only)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers: every refereed claim CORRECT, two wording fixes (REFEREE-constructive.md, REFEREE-dimers.md); li.py, the marked walk, the exchange walks and the trinity cofactors were not refereed; human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.N.O", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.N.id", "title": "spoke weights are a height function", "statement": "omega(s) is the volume under the height of s, and L+(C) - L-(C) is the number of white faces inside C, which is B + 1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md 2.3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.N.c", "title": "leading coefficient checked exactly", "statement": "The first nonzero coefficient equals the signed sum of products of enclosed face counts on every instance tested.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/supplemental.py (49 groups); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/code/linear.py; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 5 (71224 rooted triangulations up to 18 vertices)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/supplemental.py (49 groups); research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/lab/dets.py 12; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/code/linear.py; research/2026-11-14_fable_referee-determinants/code/results.json; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/REPORT.md item 5 (71224 rooted triangulations up to 18 vertices)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refd", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lean", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x1", "title": "zero, vertex-only or face-only weights", "statement": "Use weights alpha_t + beta_v, or none.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/data/zero_weights.json; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 6; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Such weights are pure gauge: every state has the same total, and the signed count is 0 = 0. What is needed is positive circulation on cycles, not positive weights.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Cube (octahedron dual, 6 vertices): two pairs with J = +1 and -1, Z = i - i = 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x2", "title": "parity or mod p count without weights", "statement": "Show the number of tree matchings is odd, or nonzero mod p.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 8; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D3; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 2; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/TABLES.md (residues mod 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The number of tree matchings is always even (the two signs balance), and T = P - 2 N_1 mod 4 is compatible with T = 0. The weighted sum is the refinement that works; the first degree at which anything survives is cmin. No modulus among 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11 gives a universally nonzero residue; the positive counts seen are 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 22.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Octahedron: 2 tree matchings, signed count 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x3", "title": "tree pair among the fewest-cycle pairs", "statement": "Among the pairs with the fewest D-cycles one has Q_s a forest; or every cycle cover D has a forest orientation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D2; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 7 (E2d, E3); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md O3 (a 40-vertex one-cycle cover with no tree pair)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Reversals inside one fixed cycle cover cannot be guaranteed to reach a forest pair, so a proof must move between covers. The leading coefficient is nonzero because of the fewest-cycle covers, but the surviving pairs can live in other covers. A statement that held on 1794 cases failed at the next size. (Scope as corrected by the referee.)", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 16 vertices, class 158, t0 = (2,7,3): a single 13-cycle whose two orientations both have a triangle in Q_s; its 12 tree matchings lie in two other covers. Also the octahedron with every face split in four (n = 15).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.gt", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x4", "title": "highest or lowest partnered state", "statement": "The top (bottom) partnered state of the lattice is a tree matching.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 4 (E1, E1c); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-graph-theory/ROUTES.md O1 (extremes of the whole matching lattice fail at 10 vertices)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "For an extreme s every D has all cycles one way, but reversing a cycle of Q_s changes the number of D-cycles by two and extremality does not forbid it.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3) for the highest state, and its mirror image for the lowest (the referee's correction: the author's enumeration identified reflections and reported 14).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x5", "title": "minimal cover, all cycles one way", "statement": "Take D with cmin cycles and orient all of them counterclockwise (or clockwise).", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 5 (E2, E2c); research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics/REFEREE.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "The leading coefficient sums over all minimal covers and prefers no orientation.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3) for counterclockwise, and its mirror image for clockwise (referee's correction; the author reported 13).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x6", "title": "largest rank difference", "statement": "The pair maximising omega(s) - omega(r) is a forest pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 6 (E5)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Maximality forces the cycles of Q_s to be counterclockwise and nothing more.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 12 vertices, class 6, t0 = (2,7,3).", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x7", "title": "one cycle always suffices", "statement": "cmin = 1, so a first-order argument is enough.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 13"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "cmin reaches 3 without separating triangles (192 of 3374 rooted cases up to 16 vertices) and 4 with them. A first-order argument is not enough and Li's Appendix B is needed. Unboundedness of cmin is not proved.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: 9 vertices: octahedron with an octahedron glued into a face, cmin = 2.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x8", "title": "cubes of tree matchings; sign = parity of rank", "statement": "Tree matchings split into cubes of dimension cmin; or eps(s) = (-1)^omega(s) up to a constant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 9, 10"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Z(q)/(q - 1)^cmin can have mixed signs, which refutes a rank-compatible signed cube decomposition. An abstract partition into cubes of dimension cmin is refuted by cardinality (referee).", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Signs: 14 vertices, class 24, face 6, Z = -1 + 2q + q^5 - 2q^6. Cardinality: a 13-vertex instance with 6 tree matchings and cmin = 2 (refc/code/cube_cardinality.json). Sign = parity of rank fails at 8 vertices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.refc", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x9", "title": "ordinary determinant, all face variables 1", "statement": "Evaluate det(sum_t M_t) with no coefficient extraction.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md, data/exact_determinant.json; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/IDENTITIES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Without extraction a black face can supply two transitions and another none; the extra terms can cancel the answer. Testing only the cube or the octahedron would have hidden this.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual (8 vertices): squarefree coefficient 45/64 at z = 5/4, all-one evaluation 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x10", "title": "allow doubled edges (standard double dimers)", "statement": "Add a diagonal so that r and s may share edges, as in Kenyon's double-dimer determinant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/PROOF.md 3; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Nonvanishing becomes too easy: F_lambda(1) = lambda^n times the number of states, which is positive even with no pair. An SL2 connection does not kill doubled edges.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: A rooted 9-vertex gluing with 4 states, no pair, doubled value 4.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x11", "title": "positive semidefinite blocks", "statement": "Find a gauge in which the local matrices M_t are positive semidefinite, then use mixed-discriminant positivity.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 4; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/ROUTES.md 3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Each block is, after multiplication by i, Hermitian of trace zero and rank two, signature (1, 1, 0). No similarity or congruence changes that. The determinant explains the cancellation and does not replace the planar positivity.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Any black face with two or three non-root corners.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x12", "title": "Combinatorial Nullstellensatz", "statement": "Get a nonzero evaluation of F from the coefficient form of Alon's theorem.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Naming a nonzero monomial of F already names a tree matching. Substituting w = a_t b_v kills F.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Any instance: F(a_t b_v) = 0.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.N.x13", "title": "real stability of the tree-state polynomial", "statement": "The unsigned generating polynomial of tree matchings is real stable, like spanning-tree polynomials.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-algebra/PROOF.md 3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Projecting onto matchings destroys stability.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: Cube: abc + def vanishes at a = b = c = e^{i pi/6}, d = e = f = i.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.alg", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.1", "title": "mixed determinant with positive curvature", "statement": "Z = [prod z_t] det(sum z_t M_t) is n! times a mixed discriminant of rank-two blocks. Prove it nonzero from structural hypotheses.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D1; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 1"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "At a = 1 the matrix is the adjacency matrix of T[X] with a U(1) connection of holonomy i around black and -i around white triangles.", "test": "Compute rank(sum over S of W_t) against |S| on cases with and without pairs; look for a non-diagonal normalisation.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.2", "title": "2-adic evaluation at z = -1", "statement": "Choose weights with every L+ - L- odd and evaluate T's polynomial at -1.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D3"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "A count mod powers of 2 that sees the weights.", "test": "Check on the examples whether such weights exist and the value is nonzero.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.3", "title": "cycle popping, random walk", "statement": "The two moves pop cycles of Q_s and of D, as in Wilson's algorithm. Show the walk hits a tree pair fast.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md D4; research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/ALGORITHMS.md (exchange walks)"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "All 320 random and greedy trials from ten bad starts ended within ten moves (con, COMPUTED, small sample).", "test": "Measure hitting times on exchange components of growing size; look for a potential.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.4", "title": "Pfaffian gadget for the turn tensor", "statement": "Replace each black face by a planar matchgate with signature q^delta on distinct ordered corners and zero on equal corners.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 6; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would remove the coefficient extraction and give a polynomial-time evaluation.", "test": "Check the Grassmann-Pluecker identities of the six-value signature with the boundary order fixed.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.5", "title": "height potential on pairs", "statement": "A combination of the two state heights that decreases along some exchange move at every non-tree pair.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 7"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would turn existence into descent.", "test": "Search for a non-tree local minimum of each candidate on small exchange graphs.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.6", "title": "curved double-dimer connection, Lee-Yang", "statement": "Realise the loop factor -i e^{xL+} + i e^{xL-} as the trace of a non-flat connection.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 15; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 8"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Each loop factor is -2i e^{xm} sinh(x Delta/2); zeros lie on the imaginary axis loop by loop.", "test": "Solve the connection equations on two bipyramids and test trace identities on nested loops.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.7", "title": "LGV after cutting along seams", "statement": "Cut the pair diagram into non-intersecting paths and use a Lindstrom-Gessel-Viennot determinant.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 8"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "A fixed path matrix would make the sum a single determinant.", "test": "Do the cut on the cube and on the first instance with two D-cycles.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.N.8", "title": "abstract valuation theorem", "statement": "Axiomatise: a finite signed cycle system, two involutions, a positive circulation.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 17"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Would say which planar hypotheses do the work.", "test": "List the axioms and find the first one that fails on a torus or a disk with four roots.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.N", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.N.9", "title": "a test function with one sign on all covers", "statement": "There is a test function of s for which every cycle cover contributes with the same sign, so that no minimum over the number of cycles is taken.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md, open question 2"], "tags": ["step N"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "On the 479 cases with more than 2^cmin tree matchings (comb/data/rows_v16.json), search low-degree polynomials in the heights.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.N", "rel": 