lest known counterexample: Hexagonal prism dual: 3 arborescences in each colour, 2 tree matchings.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.U.x4", "title": "Yutsis partition of G", "statement": "Identify the two induced trees with a Yutsis decomposition of the cubic graph.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 11"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Different ground sets: the vertices of G against the vertices of T.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: definitional", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.1h", "title": "support of the tree-degree polynomial", "statement": "Show the target degree vector d* lies in the support of det L_H(y), from plane incidence inequalities.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 2; research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P8, P9"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "An unsigned target: no cancellation to explain. If every lattice point of the degree polytope were realised (P9), convexity would finish.", "test": "Enumerate H-trees on the cube and the hexagonal bipyramid; compare the support with the lattice points of its convex hull.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.2h", "title": "spanning-tree parity / matroid parity", "statement": "'Each black centre keeps exactly two of its three spokes' looks like the spanning tree parity problem that Feder and Subi solve in polynomial time for 2- and 3-sided faces.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/REPORT.md (leads); research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 10"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "If it is a matroid parity instance, Lovasz gives a polynomial algorithm, against 3^(N/4).", "test": "Design the gadget for one black centre and two adjacent centres; enumerate feasible parity solutions against partial spoke choices.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.hist", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.U.4h", "title": "Bernardi process, Schnyder woods, blossom trees", "statement": "A canonical tree or orientation of the map might produce a tree matching directly.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/ROUTE-IDEAS.md 4, 11, 12, 13"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "Each theory uses three colours and rooted trees on triangulations, as the target does.", "test": "On the octahedron and the hexagonal bipyramid, test every facewise corner rule for bijectivity on X and for the forest condition.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.5h", "title": "order-theoretic position in the state lattice", "statement": "Outcome (topo): the tree matchings are neither an interval nor an antichain of the clock lattice, and the top and bottom states are often tree matchings. No order-theoretic pattern was found.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_route-topology/PREDICTIONS.md P6; research/2026-11-14_sol_machinery-literature/REFORMULATIONS.md 9"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Decided on the topology agent's sample (166 lattices); a description of the subset is still missing.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.topo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.mach", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.U.6h", "title": "describe partnered Hamiltonian cycles in G alone", "statement": "There is a description, without states, of the Hamiltonian cycles of G avoiding e0* whose state has a partner.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/REPORT.md, open question 3"], "tags": ["step U"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "For the hexagonal prism list the 2 partnered and 2 unpartnered avoiding cycles and compare their face sequences; then test any candidate rule on the 176726 unpartnered cycles of the survey.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.U", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.FP", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.R.1", "title": "out-degree count", "statement": "A tree component with v vertices and a roots has v - a out-edges and v - 1 edges, so a = 1. T: s is a tree matching iff it has exactly one partner.", "where": ["O Lemma 6.1; L Lemma 8; T (3), Prop. 2.1, Thm 1.2"], "tags": ["step R"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.R", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.IT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.R.c", "title": "unique partner checked on 140358 states", "statement": "Brute force over all states: