rint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "h.E.2", "title": "Temperley / Kenyon-Propp-Wilson", "statement": "Read the step as the tree-to-matching bijection of KPW.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md E2; research/2026-11-14_astra_route-dimers/ROUTES.md"], "tags": ["step E"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "hunch", "tier": "T6", "status": "live", "vivid": "KPW applied to the white graph encodes all its spanning trees and carries the label constraints along; it does not identify those dimers with B (dim).", "test": "Write the bijection for the octahedron and the n = 15 example.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.E", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.dim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.WT", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.E2.1", "title": "orient towards y0", "statement": "Each tree edge is assigned to its end farther from y0 and selects the side of its black face bordering that end.", "where": ["O 6.1; L Claim 31; T 7.1"], "tags": ["step E2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.E2.2", "title": "the three papers select the same P", "statement": "Li's trace of the dual tree through black vertices gives the same set of edges of G.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/correspondence.md 3.6"], "tags": ["step E2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.E2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.SE", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.F.OT", "title": "P is a forest, by the disk identity", "statement": "A cycle in P0 would be directed, and the selected-side count gives a disk with one black face fewer than the state requires. Then duality gives the cycle and the Jordan curve the two induced trees.", "where": ["O Lemma 6.2; T Lemma 7.1"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.F.L", "title": "innermost cycle, no disk identity", "statement": "If the complement had two cycles, an innermost one with no root face inside bounds a tree of faces, each with an out-step; some step is undone and two faces sit on one black vertex.", "where": ["L Lemma 30"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.F.1", "title": "W - B = 1 against W - B = 3", "statement": "The disk-identity argument restated as two incompatible counts of white minus black faces.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Section 5"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}, {"to": "th.F.OT", "rel": "modifies"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.F.2", "title": "forest certificate implies Hamiltonian cycle", "statement": "Conditional conversion: a spanning forest selecting one side per face has a complementary dual that is a Hamiltonian cycle.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_exposition-method/DEPENDENCY-AUDIT.md"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.expo", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.F.3", "title": "recovery is injective, with known image", "statement": "For fixed t0 and e0 the map from tree matchings to cycles is injective. Its image is the set of avoiding cycles whose state is a tree matching.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md; research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics/PROOF.md Section 6"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (1 independent AI referee; human check pending)", "review": {"state": "refereed", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_referee-combinatorics"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_fable_route-combinatorics: FOLLOWS, with corrections to domain, normalisation and the scope of the negative conclusions (REFEREE.md); human check pending. Not covered by that verdict: 2026-11-14_astra_limits"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.comb", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "c.F.c", "title": "recovery checked on every tree matching", "statement": "Every selected P is a two-component forest and both sides induce trees.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md (744 recoveries); research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/code/campaign.py 14 (3618 certificates)"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "evidence", "tier": "T4", "status": "computed", "evidence": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_route-constructive/VERIFICATION.md (744 recoveries); research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/code/campaign.py 14 (3618 certificates)"], "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.con", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.JC", "rel": "tests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.F.4", "title": "remove a leaf of the white tree", "statement": "Removing a leaf of the white tree with the black face whose spoke it crosses leaves a rooted triangulation with a tree matching, and the cycle of the larger graph is a local detour.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md F1"], "tags": ["step F"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Implement leaf removal on the trees produced by dep/scripts/check_nodes.py and check validity of the smaller object.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.F", "rel