e", "statement": "Cut at a separating triangle, cap, solve one side, prescribe the same-label edge on the other, glue. O inducts on Theorem 2.2, L takes a minimum counterexample.", "where": ["O Section 7; L Appendix C"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.G.T", "title": "cut only at black-inner triangles", "statement": "The exact criterion says when a cut is needed.", "where": ["T 7.3"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.G.K", "title": "Kelmans' reduction (1986)", "statement": "The reduction to cyclically 4-edge-connected graphs with an (x+ y+) or avoided-edge hypothesis was known. O re-proves it without citing it for this step.", "where": ["Kelmans 1986/1994 via APSW 2016 Thm 8; Hertel 2005"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T1", "status": "established (LIT: published)", "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G.1", "title": "every separating triangle has one black side", "statement": "The state method needs no cut exactly when t0 is on the black side of every separating triangle. Changing the root or swapping colours can avoid cuts, not always.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/audit-trees.md T-F1; research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md G1"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (unreviewed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "date": "2026-11-14"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "p.G.2", "title": "the gluing needs the same-label edge", "statement": "Trees of the two pieces meet in one vertex or one edge; prescribing the cap edge supplies the agreement. The smallest separating example has 9 vertices.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_astra_limits/HYPOTHESES.md (separating triangles)"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "proof supplied (under review)", "review": {"state": "under-review", "date": "2026-11-14", "by": ["research/2026-11-14_sol_referee-structure"], "verdict": "proof in research/2026-11-14_astra_limits: pending (audit started 10:50 UTC)"}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.lim", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "x.G.x1", "title": "prescribe whatever each cut needs", "statement": "Strengthen the induction hypothesis to an arbitrary set of prescribed edges.", "where": ["Bagheri Gh. et al. 2022, proof of Thm 4.6; research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/WHAT-WAS-HARD.md 6"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "deadend", "tier": null, "status": "refuted", "lesson": "Hamiltonicity through an arbitrary prescribed edge set is NP-complete for Barnette graphs. The hypothesis must prescribe something bounded: one avoided edge.", "note": "Smallest known counterexample: reduction from Akiyama-Nishizeki-Saito instances", "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "k.G.3", "title": "a cut-free root", "statement": "Count how often some root (black face on the black side of all separating triangles, or the same with colours swapped) exists.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_fable_dependency-graph/skeleton.md G1"], "tags": ["step G"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "conjecture", "tier": "T5", "status": "open", "test": "Over generated Barnette graphs with several separating triangles, compute the fraction with a cut-free root; three triangles with alternating black sides should give the first failure.", "links": [{"to": "m.step.G", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.agent.dep", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.GL", "rel": "suggests"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.G2.1", "title": "Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 7.1", "statement": "Every Barnette graph has a Hamiltonian cycle avoiding any prescribed edge.", "where": ["O Thm 1.1, Cor. 7.1; L Thm 3; T Thm 1.1"], "tags": ["step G2"], "created": "2026-11-14", "updated": "2026-11-14", "kind": "theorem", "tier": "T2", "status": "established (LIT: 2026 preprint or its formalisation, unrefereed)", "review": {"state": "unreviewed", "verdict": "Supplied preprint or formal source; no journal review claimed."}, "links": [{"to": "m.step.G2", "rel": "instance-of"}, {"to": "src.O", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.L", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "src.T", "rel": "cites"}, {"to": "wp.HC", "rel": "supports"}], "source": "labyrinth"}, {"id": "th.G2.2", "title": "Lean formalisation (OpenAI repository)", "statement": "31 Lean files, 8936 lines, importing only Mathlib. The formal statement is the conjecture as usually stated (lean/DIFFERENCES.md A). Corollary 7.2 and Theorem 2.2 are not formalised.", "where": ["research/2026-11-14_opus_history-literature/REPORT.md; research/2026-11-14_opus_lean-formalisation/graph/"], "tags": ["step G2"], "created": "20